601: 
602: {{if any already-assigned: "[#{{n}}]({{url}}) is already assigned to Copilot."}}
603: ```
604: 
605: **Template rules:**
606: 
607: - Do not include a separate "Executive Summary" section. The Triage summary + Module issues analysed at the top are the summary.
608: - Use only 3 priority tiers: 🔴 High, 🟡 Medium, ⚪ Low. No "Med-High" or intermediate tiers - if in doubt, round up to High.
609: - Drop the "% unblocked delegate" column from the breakdown table; the Copilot-ready-now count in the Triage summary is sufficient.
610: - Column headers in the per-module table must match the Triage summary vocabulary: **Copilot-ready now**, **Copilot-ready (blocked)**, **Needs owner**. Do not use "Delegate" / "Human" column names.
611: - If a chain section (duplicates, verify-and-close, document-close, PR-in-flight) is empty, omit the section entirely rather than leaving an empty table.
612: - Every issue reference must be a markdown link to its GitHub URL on first mention in each section. Use bare `#N` for repeat references inside the same row.
613: - In the "Ordering / ship-together chains" and "Open questions for you" sections, link **every** `#N` reference - these sections are scanned for clickable navigation, so do not leave bare issue numbers.
614: - Keep "Open questions" to decisions only the owner can make (ownership, design trade-offs, ping-vs-close). Do not ask what the agent can infer from the thread.
615: - Place the report at the path the caller specifies. If none is given, default to `./avm-triage-<owner_alias>-<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` in the current working directory (see Quick Start).
616: - Include the `**Mode:**` line directly under the title; this is mandatory so consumers know whether dependency edges are evidence-backed (deep) or thread-claimed (quick).
617: - In the "All Issues - Flat List" section, produce one table per repo (H3 subsection headed `` ### `Azure/{{repo}}` ({{open_count}} open) ``), and sort rows within each table by priority descending (🔴 → 🟡 → ⚪), then by issue number ascending. Order the repo subsections themselves by total open issue count descending. Do not produce a single combined table.
618: 
619: ---
620: 
621: ## Appendix A - AVM Bot Labels
622: 
623: | Label | Meaning |
624: |-------|---------|
625: | `Needs: Triage 🔍` | Not yet reviewed by maintainer |
626: | `Status: Response Overdue 🚩` | No response within SLA |
627: | `Needs: Immediate Attention ‼️` | Further escalated |
628: 
629: ## Appendix B - Useful Commands
630: 
631: ```bash
632: # Harvest open issues (dedicated repos)
633: gh issue list --repo Azure/<repo> --state open --limit 200 \
634:   --json number,title,labels,assignees,createdAt,updatedAt
635: 
636: # Authenticated curl fallback (after `gh auth refresh -s read:org` for SSO)
637: curl -sS -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gh auth token)" \
638:   "https://api.github.com/repos/Azure/<repo>/issues?state=open&per_page=100"
639: 
640: # Bicep shared repo - search body+title for slash path
641: q='repo:Azure/bicep-registry-modules is:issue is:open "avm/res/<path>"'
642: curl -sS "https://api.github.com/search/issues?q=$(python3 -c 'import urllib.parse,sys;print(urllib.parse.quote(sys.argv[1]))' "$q")&per_page=100"
643: 
644: # Deep-read (issue body + comments)
645: gh issue view <number> --repo Azure/<repo> --comments
646: # or
647: curl -sS "https://api.github.com/repos/Azure/<repo>/issues/<number>"
648: curl -sS "https://api.github.com/repos/Azure/<repo>/issues/<number>/comments"
649: 
650: # Confirm state of a previously-tracked issue (closed? re-opened?)
651: curl -sS "https://api.github.com/repos/Azure/<repo>/issues/<number>" \
652:   | python3 -c "import sys,json;d=json.load(sys.stdin);print(d['state'],d.get('closed_at'))"
653: 
654: # Assign Copilot (only after user approval)
655: gh issue edit <number> --repo Azure/<repo> --add-assignee app/copilot
656: ```
657: 
658: ## Appendix C - Authentication, Rate-Limit & SSO Survival
659: 
660: **Authenticate `gh` first.** Always prefer an authenticated `gh` session over unauthenticated `curl`:
661: 
662: ```bash
663: # One-time login (opens browser)
664: gh auth login -h github.com -p https -w
665: 
666: # Authorize SAML/SSO for the Azure org (required for Azure/* repos)
667: gh auth refresh -h github.com -s read:org
668: gh auth status   # confirm "Token scopes" includes the org under SSO
669: ```
670: 
671: If `gh` commands against `Azure/*` return `SAML enforcement`, open the URL printed by `gh` and click **Authorize** for the Azure SSO session, then re-run. The higher authenticated rate limit (5000 req/h) is needed for any non-trivial triage run.
672: 
673: - **Multiple `gh` accounts:** `gh auth status` shows all logged-in accounts. If the active account is not SSO-authorized for the Azure org but another account is, switch with `gh auth switch --user <authorized-account>` before harvesting. Check with: `gh issue list --repo Azure/bicep-registry-modules --limit 1` - a clean result confirms SSO is good for this session.
674: 
675: - **Authenticated `curl` fallback:** if you must use `curl` (scripts, Search API), pass the token so you get the 5000/h limit and access to org-gated content:
676:   ```bash
677:   curl -sS -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gh auth token)" \
678:     "https://api.github.com/repos/Azure/<repo>/issues?state=open&per_page=100"
679:   ```
680: - **Unauthenticated `curl` is last-resort only:** works for public repos but hits the 60 req/h anonymous limit fast and will not see SSO-gated content. Do not use for a full triage.
681: - **Secondary rate limit on Search API:** sleep ≥7s between search queries even when authenticated.
682: - **Large JSON outputs:** pipe through `python3 -c` to filter early; don't dump raw JSON into the triage workspace.
</file>

