27: ## Testing & validation
28: 
29: - Use tool `#runCommands` to run the command for restoring modules: `bicep restore` (required for AVM br/public:\*).
30: - Use tool `#runCommands` to run the command for bicep build (--stdout is required): `bicep build {path to bicep file}.bicep --stdout --no-restore`
31: - Use tool `#runCommands` to run the command to format the template: `bicep format {path to bicep file}.bicep`
32: - Use tool `#runCommands` to run the command to lint the template: `bicep lint {path to bicep file}.bicep`
33: - After any command check if the command failed, diagnose why it's failed using tool `#terminalLastCommand` and retry. Treat warnings from analysers as actionable.
34: - After a successful `bicep build`, remove any transient ARM JSON files created during testing.
35: 
36: ## The final check
37: 
38: - All parameters (`param`), variables (`var`) and types are used; remove dead code.
39: - AVM versions or API versions match the plan.
40: - No secrets or environment-specific values hardcoded.
41: - The generated Bicep compiles cleanly and passes format checks.
</file>

