  5: 
  6: # Azure Verified Modules (AVM) Terraform
  7: 
  8: ## Overview
  9: 
 10: Azure Verified Modules (AVM) are pre-built, tested, and validated Terraform and Bicep modules that follow Azure best practices. Use these modules to create, update, or review Azure Infrastructure as Code (IaC) with confidence.
 11: 
 12: ## Custom Instructions for GitHub Copilot Agents
 13: 
 14: **IMPORTANT**: When GitHub Copilot Agent or GitHub Copilot Coding Agent is working on this repository, the following local unit tests MUST be executed to comply with PR checks. Failure to run these tests will cause PR validation failures:
 15: 
 16: ```bash
 17: ./avm pre-commit
 18: ./avm tflint
 19: ./avm pr-check
 20: ```
 21: 
 22: These commands must be run before any pull request is created or updated to ensure compliance with the Azure Verified Modules standards and prevent CI/CD pipeline failures.
 23: More details on the AVM process can be found in the [Azure Verified Modules Contribution documentation](https://azure.github.io/Azure-Verified-Modules/contributing/terraform/testing/).
 24: 
 25: **Failure to run these tests will cause PR validation failures and prevent successful merges.**
 26: 
 27: ## Module Discovery
 28: 
 29: ### Terraform Registry
 30: 
 31: - Search for "avm" + resource name
 32: - Filter by "Partner" tag to find official AVM modules
 33: - Example: Search "avm storage account" → filter by Partner
 34: 
 35: ### Official AVM Index
 36: 
 37: > **Note:** The following links always point to the latest version of the CSV files on the main branch. As intended, this means the files may change over time. If you require a point-in-time version, consider using a specific release tag in the URL.
 38: 
 39: - **Terraform Resource Modules**: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/Azure-Verified-Modules/refs/heads/main/docs/static/module-indexes/TerraformResourceModules.csv`
 40: - **Terraform Pattern Modules**: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/Azure-Verified-Modules/refs/heads/main/docs/static/module-indexes/TerraformPatternModules.csv`
 41: - **Terraform Utility Modules**: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/Azure-Verified-Modules/refs/heads/main/docs/static/module-indexes/TerraformUtilityModules.csv`
 42: 
 43: 
 44: ## Terraform Module Usage
 45: 
 46: ### From Examples
 47: 
 48: 1. Copy the example code from the module documentation
 49: 2. Replace `source = "../../"` with `source = "Azure/avm-res-{service}-{resource}/azurerm"`
 50: 3. Add `version = "~> 1.0"` (use latest available)
 51: 4. Set `enable_telemetry = true`
 52: 
 53: ### From Scratch
 54: 
 55: 1. Copy the Provision Instructions from module documentation
 56: 2. Configure required and optional inputs
 57: 3. Pin the module version
 58: 4. Enable telemetry
 59: 
 60: ### Example Usage
 61: 
 62: ```hcl
 63: module "storage_account" {
 64:   source  = "Azure/avm-res-storage-storageaccount/azurerm"
 65:   version = "~> 0.1"
 66: 
 67:   enable_telemetry    = true
 68:   location            = "East US"
 69:   name                = "mystorageaccount"
 70:   resource_group_name = "my-rg"
 71: 
 72:   # Additional configuration...
 73: }
 74: ```
 75: 
 76: ## Naming Conventions
 77: 
 78: ### Module Types
 79: 
 80: - **Resource Modules**: `Azure/avm-res-{service}-{resource}/azurerm`
 81:   - Example: `Azure/avm-res-storage-storageaccount/azurerm`
 82: - **Pattern Modules**: `Azure/avm-ptn-{pattern}/azurerm`
 83:   - Example: `Azure/avm-ptn-aks-enterprise/azurerm`
 84: - **Utility Modules**: `Azure/avm-utl-{utility}/azurerm`
 85:   - Example: `Azure/avm-utl-regions/azurerm`
 86: 
 87: ### Service Naming
 88: 
 89: - Use kebab-case for services and resources
 90: - Follow Azure service names (e.g., `storage-storageaccount`, `network-virtualnetwork`)
 91: 
 92: ## Version Management
 93: 
 94: ### Check Available Versions
 95: 
 96: - Endpoint: `https://registry.terraform.io/v1/modules/Azure/{module}/azurerm/versions`
 97: - Example: `https://registry.terraform.io/v1/modules/Azure/avm-res-storage-storageaccount/azurerm/versions`
 98: 
 99: ### Version Pinning Best Practices
100: 
101: - Use pessimistic version constraints: `version = "~> 1.0"`
102: - Pin to specific versions for production: `version = "1.2.3"`
103: - Always review changelog before upgrading
104: 
105: ## Module Sources
106: 
107: ### Terraform Registry
108: 
109: - **URL Pattern**: `https://registry.terraform.io/modules/Azure/{module}/azurerm/latest`
110: - **Example**: `https://registry.terraform.io/modules/Azure/avm-res-storage-storageaccount/azurerm/latest`
111: 
112: ### GitHub Repository
113: 
114: - **URL Pattern**: `https://github.com/Azure/terraform-azurerm-avm-{type}-{service}-{resource}`
115: - **Examples**:
116:   - Resource: `https://github.com/Azure/terraform-azurerm-avm-res-storage-storageaccount`
117:   - Pattern: `https://github.com/Azure/terraform-azurerm-avm-ptn-aks-enterprise`
118: 
119: ## Development Best Practices
120: 
121: ### Module Usage
122: 
123: - ✅ **Always** pin module and provider versions
124: - ✅ **Start** with official examples from module documentation
125: - ✅ **Review** all inputs and outputs before implementation
126: - ✅ **Enable** telemetry: `enable_telemetry = true`
127: - ✅ **Use** AVM utility modules for common patterns
128: - ✅ **Follow** AzureRM provider requirements and constraints
129: 
130: ### Code Quality
131: 
132: - ✅ **Always** run `terraform fmt` after making changes
133: - ✅ **Always** run `terraform validate` after making changes
134: - ✅ **Use** meaningful variable names and descriptions
135: - ✅ **Add** proper tags and metadata
136: - ✅ **Document** complex configurations
137: 
138: ### Validation Requirements
139: 
140: Before creating or updating any pull request:
141: 
142: ```bash
143: # Format code
144: terraform fmt -recursive
145: 
146: # Validate syntax
147: terraform validate
148: 
149: # AVM-specific validation (MANDATORY)
150: ./avm pre-commit
151: ./avm tflint
152: ./avm pr-check
153: ```
154: 
155: ## Tool Integration
156: 
157: ### Use Available Tools
158: 
159: - **Deployment Guidance**: Use `azure_get_deployment_best_practices` tool
160: - **Service Documentation**: Use `microsoft.docs.mcp` tool for Azure service-specific guidance
161: - **Schema Information**: Use `azure_get_schema_for_Bicep` for Bicep resources
162: 
163: ### GitHub Copilot Integration
164: 
165: When working with AVM repositories:
166: 
167: 1. Always check for existing modules before creating new resources
168: 2. Use the official examples as starting points
169: 3. Run all validation tests before committing
170: 4. Document any customizations or deviations from examples
171: 
172: ## Common Patterns
173: 
174: ### Resource Group Module
175: 
176: ```hcl
177: module "resource_group" {
178:   source  = "Azure/avm-res-resources-resourcegroup/azurerm"
179:   version = "~> 0.1"
180: 
181:   enable_telemetry = true
182:   location         = var.location
183:   name            = var.resource_group_name
184: }
185: ```
186: 
187: ### Virtual Network Module
188: 
189: ```hcl
190: module "virtual_network" {
191:   source  = "Azure/avm-res-network-virtualnetwork/azurerm"
192:   version = "~> 0.1"
193: 
194:   enable_telemetry    = true
195:   location            = module.resource_group.location
196:   name                = var.vnet_name
197:   resource_group_name = module.resource_group.name
198:   address_space       = ["10.0.0.0/16"]
199: }
200: ```
201: 
202: ## Troubleshooting
203: 
204: ### Common Issues
205: 
206: 1. **Version Conflicts**: Always check compatibility between module and provider versions
207: 2. **Missing Dependencies**: Ensure all required resources are created first
208: 3. **Validation Failures**: Run AVM validation tools before committing
209: 4. **Documentation**: Always refer to the latest module documentation
210: 
211: ### Support Resources
212: 
213: - **AVM Documentation**: `https://azure.github.io/Azure-Verified-Modules/`
214: - **GitHub Issues**: Report issues in the specific module's GitHub repository
215: - **Community**: Azure Terraform Provider GitHub discussions
216: 
217: ## Compliance Checklist
218: 
219: Before submitting any AVM-related code:
220: 
221: - [ ] Module version is pinned
222: - [ ] Telemetry is enabled
223: - [ ] Code is formatted (`terraform fmt`)
224: - [ ] Code is validated (`terraform validate`)
225: - [ ] AVM pre-commit checks pass (`./avm pre-commit`)
226: - [ ] TFLint checks pass (`./avm tflint`)
227: - [ ] AVM PR checks pass (`./avm pr-check`)
228: - [ ] Documentation is updated
229: - [ ] Examples are tested and working
</file>

