 8: 
 9: # Audit Integrity Skill
10: 
11: Enforces output quality, intellectual honesty, and continuous improvement across all AppSec agents.
12: 
13: ## When to Use
14: 
15: - Every security analysis, code review, threat model, or quality scan agent run
16: - Applied automatically as a post-analysis quality gate
17: - Applicable to any agent performing SAST, SCA, threat modeling, or code quality analysis
18: 
19: ## Components
20: 
21: This skill provides 7 reusable capabilities. Agents apply all 7 unless their scope excludes a specific component.
22: 
23: | Component | Reference File | Purpose |
24: |-----------|---------------|---------|
25: | Clarification Protocol | [clarification-protocol.md](references/clarification-protocol.md) | Ask ≤2 targeted questions before analysis when scope is ambiguous |
26: | Anti-Rationalization Guard | [anti-rationalization-guard.md](references/anti-rationalization-guard.md) | Table of prohibited rationalizations with mandatory responses |
27: | Self-Critique Loop | [self-critique-loop.md](references/self-critique-loop.md) | Mandatory second-pass review after initial analysis |
28: | Retry Protocol | [retry-protocol.md](references/retry-protocol.md) | Tool failure handling — retry once, then document |
29: | Non-Negotiable Behaviors | [non-negotiable-behaviors.md](references/non-negotiable-behaviors.md) | Hard rules: never fabricate, always cite evidence, report gaps |
30: | Self-Reflection Quality Gate | [self-reflection-quality-gate.md](references/self-reflection-quality-gate.md) | 1–10 scoring rubric with ≥8 threshold per category |
31: | Self-Learning System | [self-learning-system.md](references/self-learning-system.md) | Lesson/Memory templates and governance rules |
32: 
33: ## Execution Flow
34: 
35: 1. **Before analysis**: Apply Clarification Protocol if scope is ambiguous
36: 2. **During analysis**: Apply Anti-Rationalization Guard at every decision point
37: 3. **After initial pass**: Execute Self-Critique Loop (mandatory second pass)
38: 4. **On tool failure**: Apply Retry Protocol
39: 5. **Before delivery**: Run Self-Reflection Quality Gate (all categories must score ≥8)
40: 6. **After delivery**: Create Lessons/Memories for novel findings, false positives, or methodology gaps (see Self-Learning System)
41: 
42: ## Agent-Specific Adaptation
43: 
44: Each agent customizes the **Self-Critique Loop** checklist and **Self-Reflection Quality Gate** categories to match its domain. The reference files provide the base templates; agents extend them with domain-specific items.
45: 
46: ### Example extensions per agent type
47: - **SAST/SCA agents**: Add taint trace completeness and manifest coverage checks
48: - **SonarQube-style agents**: Add rating sanity check (A–E consistency with findings)
49: - **Threat modeling agents**: Add STRIDE category completeness per trust boundary
50: - **Code review agents**: Add trust boundary audit with data flow tracing
</file>

<file path=".github/skills/mcpee-boost-mcpee-backend/skills/code-review/SKILL.md">
 1: # Code Review Skill
 2: 
 3: ## Goal
 4: 
 5: Provide an evidence-based code review workflow that turns repository signals into prioritized, actionable guidance.
 6: 
 7: ## When To Use
 8: 
 9: - Use this skill when a request requires code review guidance with concrete evidence from the repository.
10: - Use this skill when trade-offs must be prioritized by risk, impact, and delivery constraints.
11: 
12: ## Required Inputs
13: 
14: - User request.
15: - Relevant specs.
16: - Project knowledge if available.
17: - Project memory if available.
18: - Provider context if available.
19: 
20: ## Procedure
21: 
22: 1. Identify the scope of the code review request and the affected components.
23: 2. Gather direct evidence from code, configuration, and project context before drawing conclusions.
24: 3. Map findings to relevant specs and classify each issue by severity and business impact.
25: 4. Propose actionable recommendations with a safe execution order and validation approach.
26: 5. Summarize confirmed facts, open risks, and next implementation steps.
27: 
28: ## Provider Needs
29: 
30: - code-navigation
31: - dependency-analysis
32: - project-memory
33: 
34: ## Output Contract
35: 
36: The response must include:
37: 
38: - Summary.
39: - Findings.
40: - Impact.
41: - Evidence.
42: - Recommended next actions.
43: 
44: ## Quality Criteria
45: 
46: - Grounded in evidence.
47: - Uses official specs.
48: - Distinguishes facts from assumptions.
49: - Prioritizes by risk and impact.
50: - Avoids unnecessary verbosity.
51: 
52: ## Failure Modes
53: 
54: - Recommendations are generic, not backed by code or configuration evidence.
55: - Critical risks are missed because assumptions are not separated from confirmed findings.
56: 
57: ## SkillOpt Notes
58: 
59: This skill can be optimized by SkillOpt. Do not place universal knowledge here if it belongs in specs/.
</file>

