279: 
280: | Resource | Style String |
281: | ---------- | ------------- |
282: | Pod | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.pod;` |
283: | Deployment | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.deploy;` |
284: | Service | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.svc;` |
285: | Ingress | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.ing;` |
286: | ConfigMap | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.cm;` |
287: | Secret | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.secret;` |
288: | PersistentVolume | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.pv;` |
289: | Namespace | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.ns;` |
290: | Node | `shape=mxgraph.kubernetes.node;` |
291: 
292: ---
293: 
294: ## Enabling Libraries in VS Code
295: 
296: Libraries are enabled inside the draw.io editor (which VS Code embeds):
297: 
298: 1. Open any `.drawio` or `.drawio.svg` file in VS Code
299: 2. Click the `+` icon in the shape panel (left sidebar) →`Search Shapes` or `More Shapes`
300: 3. Check the library you want to activate
301: 4. Shapes appear in the panel for drag-and-drop
302: 
303: Libraries are stored per-user in draw.io settings (not per-project).
304: 
305: ---
306: 
307: ## Custom Shape Library Creation
308: 
309: A custom library is an XML file with `.xml` extension loaded via `File > Open Library`:
310: 
311: ```xml
312: <mxlibrary>
313:   [
314:     {
315:       "xml": "&lt;mxCell value=\"Component\" style=\"rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;\" vertex=\"1\"&gt;&lt;mxGeometry width=\"120\" height=\"60\" as=\"geometry\" /&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;",
316:       "w": 120,
317:       "h": 60,
318:       "aspect": "fixed",
319:       "title": "My Component"
320:     }
321:   ]
322: </mxlibrary>
323: ```
324: 
325: Each shape entry contains:
326: - `xml`: XML-escaped cell definition
327: - `w` / `h`: Default width/height
328: - `aspect`: `"fixed"` to lock ratio
329: - `title`: Name shown in panel
330: 
331:     }
332:   ]
333: </mxlibrary>
334: ```
</file>

<file path=".github/skills/mcpee-boost-mcpee-backend/skills/draw-io-diagram-generator/references/style-reference.md">
  1: # draw.io Style Reference
  2: 
  3: Complete reference for the `style` attribute on `<mxCell>` elements. Styles are semicolon-delimited `key=value` pairs.
  4: 
  5: ---
  6: 
  7: ## Style Format
  8: 
  9: ```text
 10: style="key1=value1;key2=value2;key3=value3;"
 11: ```
 12: 
 13: - Keys and values are case-sensitive
 14: - Trailing semicolon is optional but recommended
 15: - Unknown keys are silently ignored
 16: - Missing keys use draw.io defaults
 17: 
 18: ---
 19: 
 20: ## Universal Style Keys
 21: 
 22: Apply to all shapes and edges.
 23: 
 24: | Key | Values | Default | Description |
 25: | ----- | -------- | --------- | ------------- |
 26: | `fillColor` | `#hex` / `none` | `#FFFFFF` | Shape fill color (draw.io default; use semantic palette for project diagrams) |
 27: | `strokeColor` | `#hex` / `none` | `#000000` | Border/line color (draw.io default; use semantic palette for project diagrams) |
 28: | `fontColor` | `#hex` | `#000000` | Text color |
 29: | `fontSize` | integer | `11` | Font size in pt |
 30: | `fontStyle` | bitmask (see below) | `0` | Bold/italic/underline |
 31: | `fontFamily` | string | `Helvetica` | Font family name |
 32: | `align` | `left`/`center`/`right` | `center` | Horizontal text alignment |
 33: | `verticalAlign` | `top`/`middle`/`bottom` | `middle` | Vertical text alignment |
 34: | `opacity` | 0–100 | `100` | Shape opacity (%) |
 35: | `shadow` | `0`/`1` | `0` | Drop shadow |
 36: | `dashed` | `0`/`1` | `0` | Dashed border |
 37: | `dashPattern` | e.g. `8 8` | — | Custom dash/gap pattern (px) |
 38: | `strokeWidth` | float | `2` | Border/line width in px |
 39: | `spacing` | integer | `2` | Padding around text (px) |
 40: | `spacingTop` | integer | `0` | Top text padding |
 41: | `spacingBottom` | integer | `0` | Bottom text padding |
 42: | `spacingLeft` | integer | `4` | Left text padding |
 43: | `spacingRight` | integer | `4` | Right text padding |
 44: | `html` | `0`/`1` | `0` | Allow HTML in label |
 45: | `whiteSpace` | `wrap`/`nowrap` | `nowrap` | Text wrapping |
 46: | `overflow` | `visible`/`hidden`/`fill` | `visible` | Text overflow behaviour |
 47: | `rotatable` | `0`/`1` | `1` | Allow rotation in editor |
 48: | `movable` | `0`/`1` | `1` | Allow move in editor |
 49: | `resizable` | `0`/`1` | `1` | Allow resize in editor |
 50: | `deletable` | `0`/`1` | `1` | Allow delete in editor |
 51: | `editable` | `0`/`1` | `1` | Allow label edit in editor |
 52: | `locked` | `0`/`1` | `0` | Lock all editing |
 53: | `nolabel` | `0`/`1` | `0` | Hide label entirely |
 54: | `noLabel` | `0`/`1` | `0` | Alias of `nolabel` |
 55: | `labelPosition` | `left`/`center`/`right` | `center` | Label anchor horizontal |
 56: | `verticalLabelPosition` | `top`/`middle`/`bottom` | `middle` | Label anchor vertical |
 57: | `imageAlign` | `left`/`center`/`right` | `center` | Image alignment |
 58: 
 59: ### `fontStyle` Bitmask Values
 60: 
 61: | Value | Effect |
 62: | ------- | -------- |
 63: | `0` | Normal |
 64: | `1` | Bold |
 65: | `2` | Italic |
 66: | `4` | Underline |
 67: | `8` | Strikethrough |
 68: 
 69: Combine by addition: `3` = bold + italic, `5` = bold + underline, `7` = bold + italic + underline.
 70: 
 71: ---
 72: 
 73: ## Shape Keys (Vertex Only)
 74: 
 75: | Key | Values | Description |
 76: | ----- | -------- | ------------- |
 77: | `shape` | see Shape Catalog | Override default rectangle shape |
 78: | `rounded` | `0`/`1` | Rounded corners on rectangle |
 79: | `arcSize` | 0–50 | Corner radius % (when `rounded=1`) |
 80: | `perimeter` | function name | Connection perimeter type |
 81: | `aspect` | `fixed` | Lock aspect ratio on resize |
 82: | `rotation` | float | Rotation in degrees |
 83: | `fixedSize` | `0`/`1` | Prevent auto-size when editing label |
 84: | `container` | `0`/`1` | Treat shape as container for children |
 85: | `collapsible` | `0`/`1` | Allow collapse/expand toggle |
 86: | `startSize` | integer | Header size in swimlane/container (px) |
 87: | `swimlaneHead` | `0`/`1` | Show swimlane header |
 88: | `swimlaneBody` | `0`/`1` | Show swimlane body |
 89: | `fillOpacity` | 0–100 | Fill-only opacity (independent of `opacity`) |
 90: | `strokeOpacity` | 0–100 | Stroke-only opacity |
 91: | `gradientColor` | `#hex` / `none` | Gradient end color |
 92: | `gradientDirection` | `north`/`south`/`east`/`west` | Gradient direction |
 93: | `sketch` | `0`/`1` | Rough hand-drawn style |
 94: | `comic` | `0`/`1` | Comic/cartoon line style |
 95: | `glass` | `0`/`1` | Glass reflection effect |
 96: 
 97: ---
 98: 
 99: ## Shape Catalog
100: 
101: ### Basic Shapes
102: 
103: | Shape | Style String | Visual |
104: | ------- | ------------- | -------- |
105: | Rectangle (default) | *(no shape key needed)* | □ |
106: | Rounded rectangle | `rounded=1;` | ▢ |
107: | Ellipse / Circle | `ellipse;` | ○ |
108: | Diamond | `rhombus;` | ◇ |
109: | Triangle | `triangle;` | △ |
110: | Hexagon | `shape=hexagon;` | ⬡ |
111: | Pentagon | `shape=mxgraph.basic.pentagon;` | ⬠ |
112: | Star | `shape=mxgraph.basic.star;` | ★ |
