170: 
171: ## Customizing the test AppHost
172: 
173: ### Override resources
174: 
175: ```csharp
176: var builder = await DistributedApplicationTestingBuilder
177:     .CreateAsync<Projects.AppHost>();
178: 
179: // Replace a real database with a test container
180: builder.Services.ConfigureHttpClientDefaults(http =>
181: {
182:     http.AddStandardResilienceHandler();
183: });
184: 
185: // Add test-specific configuration
186: builder.Configuration["TestMode"] = "true";
187: 
188: await using var app = await builder.BuildAsync();
189: await app.StartAsync();
190: ```
191: 
192: ### Exclude resources
193: 
194: ```csharp
195: var builder = await DistributedApplicationTestingBuilder
196:     .CreateAsync<Projects.AppHost>(args =>
197:     {
198:         // Don't start the worker for API-only tests
199:         args.Args = ["--exclude-resource", "worker"];
200:     });
201: ```
202: 
203: ### Test with specific environment
204: 
205: ```csharp
206: var builder = await DistributedApplicationTestingBuilder
207:     .CreateAsync<Projects.AppHost>(args =>
208:     {
209:         args.Args = ["--environment", "Testing"];
210:     });
211: ```
212: 
213: ---
214: 
215: ## Connection string access
216: 
217: ```csharp
218: // Get the connection string for a resource in tests
219: var connectionString = await app.GetConnectionStringAsync("db");
220: 
221: // Use it to query the database directly in tests
222: using var conn = new NpgsqlConnection(connectionString);
223: await conn.OpenAsync();
224: var count = await conn.ExecuteScalarAsync<int>("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM products");
225: Assert.True(count > 0);
226: ```
227: 
228: ---
229: 
230: ## Best practices
231: 
232: 1. **Use `WaitForResourceReadyAsync`** before making requests — ensures all dependencies are healthy
233: 2. **Each test should be independent** — don't rely on state from previous tests
234: 3. **Use `await using`** for the app — ensures cleanup even on test failure
235: 4. **Test real infrastructure** — Aspire spins up real containers (Redis, PostgreSQL, etc.), giving you high-fidelity integration tests
236: 5. **Keep test AppHost lean** — exclude resources you don't need for specific test scenarios
237: 6. **Use test-specific configuration** — override settings for test isolation
238: 7. **Timeout protection** — set reasonable test timeouts since containers take time to start:
239: 
240: ```csharp
241: [Fact(Timeout = 120_000)]  // 2 minutes
242: public async Task SlowIntegrationTest() { ... }
243: ```
244: 
245: ---
246: 
247: ## Project structure
248: 
249: ```
250: MyApp/
251: ├── src/
252: │   ├── MyApp.AppHost/           # AppHost project
253: │   ├── MyApp.Api/               # API service
254: │   ├── MyApp.Worker/            # Worker service
255: │   └── MyApp.ServiceDefaults/   # Shared defaults
256: └── tests/
257:     └── MyApp.Tests/             # Integration tests
258:         ├── MyApp.Tests.csproj   # References AppHost + Testing package
259:         └── ApiTests.cs          # Test classes
260: ```
261: 
262: ```xml
263: <!-- MyApp.Tests.csproj -->
264: <Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
265:   <PropertyGroup>
266:     <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
267:     <IsAspireTestProject>true</IsAspireTestProject>
268:   </PropertyGroup>
269: 
270:   <ItemGroup>
271:     <PackageReference Include="Aspire.Hosting.Testing" Version="*" />
272:     <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="*" />
273:     <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="*" />
274:     <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="*" />
275:   </ItemGroup>
276: 
277:   <ItemGroup>
278:     <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\MyApp.AppHost\MyApp.AppHost.csproj" />
279:   </ItemGroup>
280: </Project>
281: ```
