<file path=".github/skills/mcpee-boost-mcpee-cloud/skills/aspire/references/troubleshooting.md">
  1: # Troubleshooting — Diagnostics & Common Issues
  2: 
  3: ---
  4: 
  5: ## Diagnostic Codes
  6: 
  7: Aspire emits diagnostic codes for common issues. These appear in build warnings/errors and IDE diagnostics.
  8: 
  9: ### Standard diagnostics
 10: 
 11: | Code          | Severity | Description                                                |
 12: | ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
 13: | **ASPIRE001** | Warning  | Resource name contains invalid characters                  |
 14: | **ASPIRE002** | Warning  | Duplicate resource name detected                           |
 15: | **ASPIRE003** | Error    | Missing required package reference                         |
 16: | **ASPIRE004** | Warning  | Deprecated API usage                                       |
 17: | **ASPIRE005** | Error    | Invalid endpoint configuration                             |
 18: | **ASPIRE006** | Warning  | Health check not configured for resource with `.WaitFor()` |
 19: | **ASPIRE007** | Warning  | Container image tag not specified (using `latest`)         |
 20: | **ASPIRE008** | Error    | Circular dependency detected in resource graph             |
 21: 
 22: ### Experimental diagnostics (ASPIREHOSTINGX\*)
 23: 
 24: These codes indicate usage of experimental/preview APIs. They may require `#pragma warning disable` or `<NoWarn>` if you intentionally use experimental features:
 25: 
 26: | Code                      | Area                             |
 27: | ------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
 28: | ASPIRE_HOSTINGX_0001–0005 | Experimental hosting APIs        |
 29: | ASPIRE_HOSTINGX_0006–0010 | Experimental integration APIs    |
 30: | ASPIRE_HOSTINGX_0011–0015 | Experimental deployment APIs     |
 31: | ASPIRE_HOSTINGX_0016–0022 | Experimental resource model APIs |
 32: 
 33: To suppress experimental warnings:
 34: 
 35: ```xml
 36: <!-- In .csproj -->
 37: <PropertyGroup>
 38:   <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);ASPIRE_HOSTINGX_0001</NoWarn>
 39: </PropertyGroup>
 40: ```
 41: 
 42: Or per-line:
 43: 
 44: ```csharp
 45: #pragma warning disable ASPIRE_HOSTINGX_0001
 46: var resource = builder.AddExperimentalResource("test");
 47: #pragma warning restore ASPIRE_HOSTINGX_0001
 48: ```
 49: 
 50: ---
 51: 
 52: ## Common Issues & Solutions
 53: 
 54: ### Container runtime
 55: 
 56: | Problem                           | Solution                                                                                               |
 57: | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
 58: | "Cannot connect to Docker daemon" | Start Docker Desktop / Podman / Rancher Desktop                                                        |
 59: | Container fails to start          | Check `docker ps -a` for exit codes; check dashboard console logs                                      |
 60: | Port already in use               | Another process is using the port; Aspire auto-assigns, but `targetPort` must be free on the container |
 61: | Container image pull fails        | Check network connectivity; verify image name and tag                                                  |
 62: | "Permission denied" on Linux      | Add user to `docker` group: `sudo usermod -aG docker $USER`                                            |
 63: 
 64: ### Service discovery
 65: 
 66: | Problem                       | Solution                                                                     |
 67: | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
 68: | Service can't find dependency | Verify `.WithReference()` in AppHost; check env vars in dashboard            |
 69: | Connection string is null     | The reference resource name doesn't match; check `ConnectionStrings__<name>` |
 70: | Wrong port in service URL     | Check `targetPort` vs actual service listen port                             |
 71: | Env var not set               | Rebuild AppHost; verify resource name matches exactly                        |
 72: 
 73: ### Python workloads
 74: 
 75: | Problem                           | Solution                                                        |
 76: | --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
 77: | "Python not found"                | Ensure Python is on PATH; specify full path in `AddPythonApp()` |
 78: | venv not found                    | Use `.WithVirtualEnvironment()` or create venv manually         |
 79: | pip packages fail to install      | Use `.WithPipPackages()` or install in venv before `aspire run` |
 80: | ModuleNotFoundError               | venv isn't activated; `.WithVirtualEnvironment()` handles this  |
 81: | "Port already in use" for Uvicorn | Check `targetPort` — another instance may be running            |
 82: 
 83: ### JavaScript / TypeScript workloads
 84: 
 85: | Problem                       | Solution                                                         |
 86: | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
 87: | "node_modules not found"      | Use `.WithNpmPackageInstallation()` to auto-install              |
 88: | npm install fails             | Check `package.json` is valid; check npm registry connectivity   |
 89: | Vite dev server won't start   | Verify `vite` is in devDependencies; check Vite config           |
 90: | Port mismatch                 | Ensure `targetPort` matches the port in your JS framework config |
 91: | TypeScript compilation errors | These happen in the service, not Aspire — check service logs     |
 92: 
 93: ### Go workloads
 94: 
 95: | Problem                    | Solution                                                   |
 96: | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
 97: | "go not found"             | Ensure Go is installed and on PATH                         |
 98: | Build fails                | Check `go.mod` exists in working directory                 |
 99: | "no Go files in directory" | Verify `workingDir` points to the directory with `main.go` |
100: 
101: ### Java workloads
102: 
103: | Problem                  | Solution                                                |
104: | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
105: | "java not found"         | Ensure JDK is installed and `JAVA_HOME` is set          |
106: | Maven/Gradle build fails | Verify build files exist; check build tool installation |
107: | Spring Boot won't start  | Check `application.properties`; verify main class       |
108: 
109: ### Rust workloads
110: 
111: | Problem              | Solution                                                             |
112: | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
113: | "cargo not found"    | Install Rust via rustup                                              |
114: | Build takes too long | Rust compile times are normal; use `.WithCargoBuild()` for pre-build |
115: 
116: ### Health checks & startup
117: 
118: | Problem                      | Solution                                                                       |
119: | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
120: | Resource stuck in "Starting" | Health check endpoint not responding; check service logs                       |
121: | `.WaitFor()` timeout         | Increase timeout or fix health endpoint; default is 30 seconds                 |
122: | Health check always fails    | Verify endpoint path (default: `/health`); check service binds to correct port |
123: | Cascading startup failures   | A dependency failed; check the root resource first                             |
124: 
125: ### Dashboard
126: 
127: | Problem                               | Solution                                                                  |
128: | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
129: | Dashboard doesn't open                | Check terminal for URL; use `--dashboard-port` for fixed port             |
130: | No logs appearing                     | Service may not be writing to stdout/stderr; check console output         |
131: | No traces for non-.NET services       | Configure OpenTelemetry SDK in the service; see [Dashboard](dashboard.md) |
132: | Traces don't show cross-service calls | Propagate trace context headers (`traceparent`, `tracestate`)             |
133: 
134: ### Build & configuration
135: 
136: | Problem                                   | Solution                                                            |
137: | ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
138: | "Project not found" for `AddProject<T>()` | Ensure `.csproj` is in the solution and referenced by AppHost       |
139: | Package version conflicts                 | Pin all Aspire packages to the same version                         |
140: | AppHost won't build                       | Check `Aspire.AppHost.Sdk` is in the project; run `dotnet restore`  |
141: | `aspire run` build error                  | Fix the build error first; `aspire run` requires a successful build |
142: 
143: ### Deployment
144: 
145: | Problem                                  | Solution                                                             |
146: | ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
147: | `aspire publish` fails                   | Check publisher package is installed (e.g., `Aspire.Hosting.Docker`) |
148: | Generated Bicep has errors               | Check for unsupported resource configurations                        |
149: | Container image push fails               | Verify registry credentials and permissions                          |
150: | Missing connection strings in deployment | Check generated ConfigMaps/Secrets match resource names              |
151: 
152: ---
153: 
154: ## Debugging strategies
155: 
156: ### 1. Check the dashboard first
157: 
158: The dashboard shows resource state, logs, traces, and metrics. Start here for any issue.
159: 
160: ### 2. Check environment variables
161: 
162: In the dashboard, click a resource to see all injected environment variables. Verify connection strings and service URLs are correct.
163: 
164: ### 3. Read console logs
165: 
166: Dashboard → Console Logs → filter by the failing resource. Raw stdout/stderr often contains the root cause.
167: 
168: ### 4. Check the DAG
169: 
170: If services fail to start, check the dependency order. A failed dependency blocks all downstream resources.
171: 
172: ### 5. Use MCP for AI-assisted debugging
173: 
174: If MCP is configured (see [MCP Server](mcp-server.md)), ask your AI assistant:
175: 
176: - "What resources are failing?"
177: - "Show me the logs for [service]"
178: - "What traces show errors?"
179: 
180: ### 6. Isolate the problem
181: 
182: Run just the failing resource by commenting out others in the AppHost. This narrows whether the issue is the resource itself or a dependency.
183: 
184: ---
185: 
186: ## Getting help
187: 
188: | Channel                 | URL                                            |
189: | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
190: | GitHub Issues (runtime) | https://github.com/dotnet/aspire/issues        |
191: | GitHub Issues (docs)    | https://github.com/microsoft/aspire.dev/issues |
192: | Discord                 | https://aka.ms/aspire/discord                  |
193: | Stack Overflow          | Tag: `dotnet-aspire`                           |
194: | Reddit                  | https://www.reddit.com/r/aspiredotdev/         |
