27: > **Always verify child resources as well**: Child resources such as `accounts/projects`, `accounts/deployments`, `privateDnsZones/virtualNetworkLinks` may have different API versions from their parent. Follow child resource links from the parent page to verify.
28: 
29: ### Services Not in the Table Above
30: 
31: The table above includes only v1 scope services. For other services, construct the URL in this format and fetch:
32: ```
33: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/templates/microsoft.{provider}/{resourceType}
34: ```
35: 
36: ---
37: 
38: ## 2. Model Availability (Required When Using Foundry/OpenAI Models)
39: 
40: Verify whether the model name is deployable in the target region. Do not rely on static knowledge.
41: 
42: | Verification Method | URL / Command |
43: |--------------------|---------------|
44: | MS Docs model availability | https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/openai/concepts/models |
45: | Azure CLI (existing resources) | `az cognitiveservices account list-models --name "<NAME>" --resource-group "<RG>" -o table` |
46: 
47: > If the model is unavailable in the target region → Notify the user and suggest available regions/alternative models. Do not substitute without user approval.
48: 
49: ---
50: 
51: ## 3. Private Endpoint Mapping (When Adding New Services)
52: 
53: PE groupId and DNS Zone mappings can be changed by Azure. When adding new services or verification is needed:
54: 
55: | Verification Method | URL |
56: |--------------------|-----|
57: | PE DNS integration official docs | https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/private-endpoint-dns |
58: 
59: > Key service mappings in `service-gotchas.md` are stable, but always re-verify from the URL above when adding new services.
60: 
61: ---
62: 
63: ## 4. Service Region Availability
64: 
65: Verify whether a specific service is available in a specific region:
66: 
67: | Verification Method | URL |
68: |--------------------|-----|
69: | Azure service-by-region availability | https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/explore/global-infrastructure/products-by-region/ |
70: 
71: ---
72: 
73: ## 5. Azure Updates (Secondary Awareness)
74: 
75: The sources below are for **reference only**. The primary source is always MS Docs official documentation.
76: 
77: | Source | URL | Purpose |
78: |--------|-----|---------|
79: | Azure Updates | https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/ | Service change awareness |
80: | What's New in Azure | Per-service What's New pages in Docs | Feature change verification |
81: 
82: ---
83: 
84: ## Decision Rule: When to Fetch?
85: 
86: | Information Type | Must Fetch? | Rationale |
87: |-----------------|-------------|-----------|
88: | API version | **Always fetch** | Changes frequently; incorrect values cause deployment failure |
89: | Model availability (name, region) | **Always fetch** | Varies by region and changes frequently |
90: | SKU list | **Always fetch** | Can change per service |
91: | Region availability | **Always fetch** | Per-service region support changes frequently. Always verify that the user-specified region is available for the service |
92: | PE groupId & DNS Zone | Can reference `service-gotchas.md` for v1 key services; **must fetch for new services or complex configurations (Monitor, etc.)** | Key service mappings are stable, but new/complex services are risky |
93: | Required property patterns | Reference files first | Near-immutable (isHnsEnabled, etc.) |
</file>

