<file path=".github/skills/mcpee-boost-mcpee-cloud/skills/azure-deployment-preflight/references/ERROR-HANDLING.md">
  1: # Error Handling Guide
  2: 
  3: This reference documents common errors during preflight validation and how to handle them.
  4: 
  5: ## Core Principle
  6: 
  7: **Continue on failure.** Capture all issues in the final report rather than stopping at the first error. This gives users a complete picture of what needs to be fixed.
  8: 
  9: ---
 10: 
 11: ## Authentication Errors
 12: 
 13: ### Not Logged In (Azure CLI)
 14: 
 15: **Detection:**
 16: ```
 17: ERROR: Please run 'az login' to setup account.
 18: ERROR: AADSTS700082: The refresh token has expired
 19: ```
 20: 
 21: **Exit Codes:** Non-zero
 22: 
 23: **Handling:**
 24: 1. Note the error in the report
 25: 2. Include remediation steps
 26: 3. Skip remaining Azure CLI commands
 27: 4. Continue with other validation steps if possible
 28: 
 29: **Report Entry:**
 30: ```markdown
 31: #### ❌ Azure CLI Authentication Required
 32: 
 33: - **Severity:** Error
 34: - **Source:** az cli
 35: - **Message:** Not logged in to Azure CLI
 36: - **Remediation:** Run `az login` to authenticate, then re-run preflight validation
 37: - **Documentation:** https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/authenticate-azure-cli
 38: ```
 39: 
 40: ### Not Logged In (azd)
 41: 
 42: **Detection:**
 43: ```
 44: ERROR: not logged in, run `azd auth login` to login
 45: ```
 46: 
 47: **Handling:**
 48: 1. Note the error in the report
 49: 2. Skip azd commands
 50: 3. Suggest `azd auth login`
 51: 
 52: **Report Entry:**
 53: ```markdown
 54: #### ❌ Azure Developer CLI Authentication Required
 55: 
 56: - **Severity:** Error
 57: - **Source:** azd
 58: - **Message:** Not logged in to Azure Developer CLI
 59: - **Remediation:** Run `azd auth login` to authenticate, then re-run preflight validation
 60: ```
 61: 
 62: ### Token Expired
 63: 
 64: **Detection:**
 65: ```
 66: AADSTS700024: Client assertion is not within its valid time range
 67: AADSTS50173: The provided grant has expired
 68: ```
 69: 
 70: **Handling:**
 71: 1. Note the error
 72: 2. Suggest re-authentication
 73: 3. Skip Azure operations
 74: 
 75: ---
 76: 
 77: ## Permission Errors
 78: 
 79: ### Insufficient RBAC Permissions
 80: 
 81: **Detection:**
 82: ```
 83: AuthorizationFailed: The client '...' with object id '...' does not have authorization 
 84: to perform action '...' over scope '...'
 85: ```
 86: 
 87: **Handling:**
 88: 1. **First attempt:** Retry with `--validation-level ProviderNoRbac`
 89: 2. Note the permission limitation in the report
 90: 3. If ProviderNoRbac also fails, report the specific missing permission
 91: 
 92: **Report Entry:**
 93: ```markdown
 94: #### ⚠️ Limited Permission Validation
 95: 
 96: - **Severity:** Warning
 97: - **Source:** what-if
 98: - **Message:** Full RBAC validation failed; using read-only validation
 99: - **Detail:** Missing permission: `Microsoft.Resources/deployments/write` on scope `/subscriptions/xxx`
100: - **Recommendation:** Request Contributor role on the target resource group, or verify deployment permissions with your administrator
101: ```
102: 
103: ### Resource Group Not Found
104: 
105: **Detection:**
106: ```
107: ResourceGroupNotFound: Resource group 'xxx' could not be found.
108: ```
109: 
110: **Handling:**
111: 1. Note in report
112: 2. Suggest creating the resource group
113: 3. Skip what-if for this scope
114: 
115: **Report Entry:**
116: ```markdown
117: #### ❌ Resource Group Does Not Exist
118: 
119: - **Severity:** Error
120: - **Source:** what-if
121: - **Message:** Resource group 'my-rg' does not exist
122: - **Remediation:** Create the resource group before deployment:
123:   ```bash
124:   az group create --name my-rg --location eastus
125:   ```
126: ```
127: 
128: ### Subscription Access Denied
129: 
130: **Detection:**
131: ```
132: SubscriptionNotFound: The subscription 'xxx' could not be found.
133: InvalidSubscriptionId: Subscription '...' is not valid
134: ```
135: 
136: **Handling:**
137: 1. Note in report
138: 2. Suggest checking subscription ID
139: 3. List available subscriptions
140: 
141: ---
142: 
143: ## Bicep Syntax Errors
144: 
145: ### Compilation Errors
146: 
147: **Detection:**
148: ```
149: /path/main.bicep(22,51) : Error BCP064: Found unexpected tokens
150: /path/main.bicep(10,5) : Error BCP018: Expected the "=" character at this location
151: ```
152: 
153: **Handling:**
154: 1. Parse error output for line/column numbers
155: 2. Include all errors in report (don't stop at first)
156: 3. Continue to what-if (may provide additional context)
157: 
158: **Report Entry:**
159: ```markdown
160: #### ❌ Bicep Syntax Error
161: 
162: - **Severity:** Error
163: - **Source:** bicep build
164: - **Location:** `main.bicep:22:51`
165: - **Code:** BCP064
166: - **Message:** Found unexpected tokens in interpolated expression
167: - **Remediation:** Check the string interpolation syntax at line 22
168: - **Documentation:** https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/bicep/diagnostics/bcp064
169: ```
170: 
171: ### Module Not Found
172: 
173: **Detection:**
174: ```
175: Error BCP091: An error occurred reading file. Could not find file '...'
176: Error BCP190: The module is not valid
177: ```
178: 
179: **Handling:**
180: 1. Note missing module
181: 2. Check if `bicep restore` is needed
182: 3. Verify module path
183: 
184: ### Parameter File Issues
185: 
186: **Detection:**
187: ```
188: Error BCP032: The value must be a compile-time constant
189: Error BCP035: The specified object is missing required properties
190: ```
191: 
192: **Handling:**
193: 1. Note parameter issues
194: 2. Indicate which parameters are problematic
195: 3. Suggest fixes
196: 
197: ---
198: 
199: ## Tool Not Installed
200: 
201: ### Azure CLI Not Found
202: 
203: **Detection:**
204: ```
205: 'az' is not recognized as an internal or external command
206: az: command not found
207: ```
208: 
209: **Handling:**
210: 1. Note in report
211: 2. Provide installation instructions.
212:   - If available use the Azure MCP `extension_cli_install` tool to get installation instructions.
213:   - Otherwise look for instructions at https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli.
214: 3. Skip az commands
215: 
216: **Report Entry:**
217: ```markdown
218: #### ⏭️ Azure CLI Not Installed
219: 
220: - **Severity:** Warning
221: - **Source:** environment
222: - **Message:** Azure CLI (az) is not installed or not in PATH
223: - **Remediation:** Install the Azure CLI <ADD INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS HERE>
224: - **Impact:** What-if validation using az commands was skipped
225: ```
226: 
227: ### Bicep CLI Not Found
228: 
229: **Detection:**
230: ```
231: 'bicep' is not recognized as an internal or external command
232: bicep: command not found
233: ```
234: 
235: **Handling:**
236: 1. Note in report
237: 2. Azure CLI may have built-in Bicep - try `az bicep build`
238: 3. Provide installation link
239: 
240: **Report Entry:**
241: ```markdown
242: #### ⏭️ Bicep CLI Not Installed
243: 
244: - **Severity:** Warning
245: - **Source:** environment
246: - **Message:** Bicep CLI is not installed
247: - **Remediation:** Install Bicep CLI: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/bicep/install
248: - **Impact:** Syntax validation was skipped; Azure will validate during what-if
249: ```
250: 
251: ### Azure Developer CLI Not Found
252: 
253: **Detection:**
254: ```
255: 'azd' is not recognized as an internal or external command
256: azd: command not found
257: ```
258: 
259: **Handling:**
260: 1. If `azure.yaml` exists, this is required
261: 2. Fall back to az CLI commands if possible
262: 3. Note in report
263: 
264: ---
265: 
266: ## What-If Specific Errors
267: 
268: ### Nested Template Limits
269: 
270: **Detection:**
271: ```
272: The deployment exceeded the nested template limit of 500
273: ```
274: 
275: **Handling:**
276: 1. Note as warning (not error)
277: 2. Explain affected resources show as "Ignore"
278: 3. Suggest manual review
279: 
280: ### Template Link Not Supported
281: 
282: **Detection:**
283: ```
284: templateLink references in nested deployments won't be visible in what-if
285: ```
286: 
287: **Handling:**
288: 1. Note as warning
289: 2. Explain limitation
290: 3. Resources will be verified during actual deployment
291: 
292: ### Unevaluated Expressions
293: 
294: **Detection:** Properties showing function names like `[utcNow()]` instead of values
295: 
296: **Handling:**
297: 1. Note as informational
298: 2. Explain these are evaluated at deployment time
299: 3. Not an error
300: 
301: ---
302: 
303: ## Network Errors
304: 
305: ### Timeout
306: 
307: **Detection:**
308: ```
309: Connection timed out
310: Request timed out
311: ```
312: 
313: **Handling:**
314: 1. Suggest retry
315: 2. Check network connectivity
316: 3. May indicate Azure service issues
317: 
318: ### SSL/TLS Errors
319: 
320: **Detection:**
321: ```
322: SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED
323: unable to get local issuer certificate
324: ```
325: 
326: **Handling:**
327: 1. Note in report
328: 2. May indicate proxy or corporate firewall
329: 3. Suggest checking SSL settings
330: 
331: ---
332: 
333: ## Fallback Strategy
334: 
335: When primary validation fails, attempt fallbacks in order:
336: 
337: ```
338: Provider (full RBAC validation)
339:     ↓ fails with permission error
340: ProviderNoRbac (validation without write permission check)
341:     ↓ fails
342: Template (static syntax only)
343:     ↓ fails
344: Report all failures and skip what-if analysis
345: ```
346: 
347: **Always continue to generate the report**, even if all validation steps fail.
348: 
349: ---
350: 
351: ## Error Report Aggregation
352: 
353: When multiple errors occur, aggregate them logically:
354: 
355: 1. **Group by source** (bicep, what-if, permissions)
356: 2. **Order by severity** (errors before warnings)
357: 3. **Deduplicate** similar errors
358: 4. **Provide summary count** at the top
359: 
360: Example:
361: ```markdown
362: ## Issues
363: 
364: Found **3 errors** and **2 warnings**
365: 
366: ### Errors (3)
367: 
368: 1. [Bicep Syntax Error - main.bicep:22:51](#error-1)
369: 2. [Bicep Syntax Error - main.bicep:45:10](#error-2)
370: 3. [Resource Group Not Found](#error-3)
371: 
372: ### Warnings (2)
373: 
374: 1. [Limited Permission Validation](#warning-1)
375: 2. [Nested Template Limit Reached](#warning-2)
376: ```
377: 
378: ---
379: 
380: ## Exit Code Reference
381: 
382: | Tool | Exit Code | Meaning |
383: |------|-----------|---------|
384: | az | 0 | Success |
385: | az | 1 | General error |
386: | az | 2 | Command not found |
387: | az | 3 | Required argument missing |
388: | azd | 0 | Success |
389: | azd | 1 | Error |
390: | bicep | 0 | Build succeeded |
391: | bicep | 1 | Build failed (errors) |
392: | bicep | 2 | Build succeeded with warnings |
</file>

