  2: name: azure-deployment-preflight
  3: description: 'Performs comprehensive preflight validation of Bicep deployments to Azure, including template syntax validation, what-if analysis, and permission checks. Use this skill before any deployment to Azure to preview changes, identify potential issues, and ensure the deployment will succeed. Activate when users mention deploying to Azure, validating Bicep files, checking deployment permissions, previewing infrastructure changes, running what-if, or preparing for azd provision.'
  4: ---
  5: 
  6: # Azure Deployment Preflight Validation
  7: 
  8: This skill validates Bicep deployments before execution, supporting both Azure CLI (`az`) and Azure Developer CLI (`azd`) workflows.
  9: 
 10: ## When to Use This Skill
 11: 
 12: - Before deploying infrastructure to Azure
 13: - When preparing or reviewing Bicep files
 14: - To preview what changes a deployment will make
 15: - To verify permissions are sufficient for deployment
 16: - Before running `azd up`, `azd provision`, or `az deployment` commands
 17: 
 18: ## Validation Process
 19: 
 20: Follow these steps in order. Continue to the next step even if a previous step fails—capture all issues in the final report.
 21: 
 22: ### Step 1: Detect Project Type
 23: 
 24: Determine the deployment workflow by checking for project indicators:
 25: 
 26: 1. **Check for azd project**: Look for `azure.yaml` in the project root
 27:    - If found → Use **azd workflow**
 28:    - If not found → Use **az CLI workflow**
 29: 
 30: 2. **Locate Bicep files**: Find all `.bicep` files to validate
 31:    - For azd projects: Check `infra/` directory first, then project root
 32:    - For standalone: Use the file specified by the user or search common locations (`infra/`, `deploy/`, project root)
 33: 
 34: 3. **Auto-detect parameter files**: For each Bicep file, look for matching parameter files:
 35:    - `<filename>.bicepparam` (Bicep parameters - preferred)
 36:    - `<filename>.parameters.json` (JSON parameters)
 37:    - `parameters.json` or `parameters/<env>.json` in same directory
 38: 
 39: ### Step 2: Validate Bicep Syntax
 40: 
 41: Run Bicep CLI to check template syntax before attempting deployment validation:
 42: 
 43: ```bash
 44: bicep build <bicep-file> --stdout
 45: ```
 46: 
 47: **What to capture:**
 48: - Syntax errors with line/column numbers
 49: - Warning messages
 50: - Build success/failure status
 51: 
 52: **If Bicep CLI is not installed:**
 53: - Note the issue in the report
 54: - Continue to Step 3 (Azure will validate syntax during what-if)
 55: 
 56: ### Step 3: Run Preflight Validation
 57: 
 58: Choose the appropriate validation based on project type detected in Step 1.
 59: 
 60: #### For azd Projects (azure.yaml exists)
 61: 
 62: Use `azd provision --preview` to validate the deployment:
 63: 
 64: ```bash
 65: azd provision --preview
 66: ```
 67: 
 68: If an environment is specified or multiple environments exist:
 69: ```bash
 70: azd provision --preview --environment <env-name>
 71: ```
 72: 
 73: #### For Standalone Bicep (no azure.yaml)
 74: 
 75: Determine the deployment scope from the Bicep file's `targetScope` declaration:
 76: 
 77: | Target Scope | Command |
 78: |--------------|---------|
 79: | `resourceGroup` (default) | `az deployment group what-if` |
 80: | `subscription` | `az deployment sub what-if` |
 81: | `managementGroup` | `az deployment mg what-if` |
 82: | `tenant` | `az deployment tenant what-if` |
 83: 
 84: **Run with Provider validation level first:**
 85: 
 86: ```bash
 87: # Resource Group scope (most common)
 88: az deployment group what-if \
 89:   --resource-group <rg-name> \
 90:   --template-file <bicep-file> \
 91:   --parameters <param-file> \
 92:   --validation-level Provider
 93: 
 94: # Subscription scope
 95: az deployment sub what-if \
 96:   --location <location> \
 97:   --template-file <bicep-file> \
 98:   --parameters <param-file> \
 99:   --validation-level Provider
100: 
101: # Management Group scope
102: az deployment mg what-if \
103:   --location <location> \
104:   --management-group-id <mg-id> \
105:   --template-file <bicep-file> \
106:   --parameters <param-file> \
107:   --validation-level Provider
108: 
109: # Tenant scope
110: az deployment tenant what-if \
111:   --location <location> \
112:   --template-file <bicep-file> \
113:   --parameters <param-file> \
114:   --validation-level Provider
115: ```
116: 
117: **Fallback Strategy:**
118: 
119: If `--validation-level Provider` fails with permission errors (RBAC), retry with `ProviderNoRbac`:
120: 
121: ```bash
122: az deployment group what-if \
123:   --resource-group <rg-name> \
124:   --template-file <bicep-file> \
125:   --validation-level ProviderNoRbac
126: ```
127: 
128: Note the fallback in the report—the user may lack full deployment permissions.
129: 
130: ### Step 4: Capture What-If Results
131: 
132: Parse the what-if output to categorize resource changes:
133: 
134: | Change Type | Symbol | Meaning |
135: |-------------|--------|---------|
136: | Create | `+` | New resource will be created |
137: | Delete | `-` | Resource will be deleted |
138: | Modify | `~` | Resource properties will change |
139: | NoChange | `=` | Resource unchanged |
140: | Ignore | `*` | Resource not analyzed (limits reached) |
141: | Deploy | `!` | Resource will be deployed (changes unknown) |
142: 
143: For modified resources, capture the specific property changes.
144: 
145: ### Step 5: Generate Report
146: 
147: Create a Markdown report file in the **project root** named:
148: - `preflight-report.md`
149: 
150: Use the template structure from [references/REPORT-TEMPLATE.md](references/REPORT-TEMPLATE.md).
151: 
152: **Report sections:**
153: 1. **Summary** - Overall status, timestamp, files validated, target scope
154: 2. **Tools Executed** - Commands run, versions, validation levels used
155: 3. **Issues** - All errors and warnings with severity and remediation
156: 4. **What-If Results** - Resources to create/modify/delete/unchanged
157: 5. **Recommendations** - Actionable next steps
158: 
159: ## Required Information
160: 
161: Before running validation, gather:
162: 
163: | Information | Required For | How to Obtain |
164: |-------------|--------------|---------------|
165: | Resource Group | `az deployment group` | Ask user or check existing `.azure/` config |
166: | Subscription | All deployments | `az account show` or ask user |
167: | Location | Sub/MG/Tenant scope | Ask user or use default from config |
168: | Environment | azd projects | `azd env list` or ask user |
169: 
170: If required information is missing, prompt the user before proceeding.
171: 
172: ## Error Handling
173: 
174: See [references/ERROR-HANDLING.md](references/ERROR-HANDLING.md) for detailed error handling guidance.
175: 
176: **Key principle:** Continue validation even when errors occur. Capture all issues in the final report.
177: 
178: | Error Type | Action |
179: |------------|--------|
180: | Not logged in | Note in report, suggest `az login` or `azd auth login` |
181: | Permission denied | Fall back to `ProviderNoRbac`, note in report |
182: | Bicep syntax error | Include all errors, continue to other files |
183: | Tool not installed | Note in report, skip that validation step |
184: | Resource group not found | Note in report, suggest creating it |
185: 
186: ## Tool Requirements
187: 
188: This skill uses the following tools:
189: 
190: - **Azure CLI** (`az`) - Version 2.76.0+ recommended for `--validation-level`
191: - **Azure Developer CLI** (`azd`) - For projects with `azure.yaml`
192: - **Bicep CLI** (`bicep`) - For syntax validation
193: - **Azure MCP Tools** - For documentation lookups and best practices
194: 
195: Check tool availability before starting:
196: ```bash
197: az --version
198: azd version
199: bicep --version
200: ```
201: 
202: ## Example Workflow
203: 
204: 1. User: "Validate my Bicep deployment before I run it"
205: 2. Agent detects `azure.yaml` → azd project
206: 3. Agent finds `infra/main.bicep` and `infra/main.bicepparam`
207: 4. Agent runs `bicep build infra/main.bicep --stdout`
208: 5. Agent runs `azd provision --preview`
209: 6. Agent generates `preflight-report.md` in project root
210: 7. Agent summarizes findings to user
211: 
212: ## Reference Documentation
213: 
214: - [Validation Commands Reference](references/VALIDATION-COMMANDS.md)
215: - [Report Template](references/REPORT-TEMPLATE.md)
216: - [Error Handling Guide](references/ERROR-HANDLING.md)
</file>

