 10: ## Work Items (Boards)
 11: 
 12: ### Query Work Items
 13: 
 14: ```bash
 15: # WIQL query
 16: az boards query \
 17:   --wiql "SELECT [System.Id], [System.Title], [System.State] FROM WorkItems WHERE [System.AssignedTo] = @Me AND [System.State] = 'Active'"
 18: 
 19: # Query with output format
 20: az boards query --wiql "SELECT * FROM WorkItems" --output table
 21: ```
 22: 
 23: ### Show Work Item
 24: 
 25: ```bash
 26: az boards work-item show --id {work-item-id}
 27: az boards work-item show --id {work-item-id} --open
 28: ```
 29: 
 30: ### Create Work Item
 31: 
 32: ```bash
 33: # Basic work item
 34: az boards work-item create \
 35:   --title "Fix login bug" \
 36:   --type Bug \
 37:   --assigned-to user@example.com \
 38:   --description "Users cannot login with SSO"
 39: 
 40: # With area and iteration
 41: az boards work-item create \
 42:   --title "New feature" \
 43:   --type "User Story" \
 44:   --area "Project\\Area1" \
 45:   --iteration "Project\\Sprint 1"
 46: 
 47: # With custom fields
 48: az boards work-item create \
 49:   --title "Task" \
 50:   --type Task \
 51:   --fields "Priority=1" "Severity=2"
 52: 
 53: # With discussion comment
 54: az boards work-item create \
 55:   --title "Issue" \
 56:   --type Bug \
 57:   --discussion "Initial investigation completed"
 58: 
 59: # For a long --discussion body on Windows, see references/long-comments-on-windows.md.
 60: # Short version: use azps.ps1 in PowerShell, or fall back to 'az devops invoke'
 61: # with --in-file when no native --file-path flag is available.
 62: 
 63: # Open in browser after creation
 64: az boards work-item create --title "Bug" --type Bug --open
 65: ```
 66: 
 67: ### Update Work Item
 68: 
 69: ```bash
 70: # Update state, title, and assignee
 71: az boards work-item update \
 72:   --id {work-item-id} \
 73:   --state "Active" \
 74:   --title "Updated title" \
 75:   --assigned-to user@example.com
 76: 
 77: # Move to different area
 78: az boards work-item update \
 79:   --id {work-item-id} \
 80:   --area "{ProjectName}\\{Team}\\{Area}"
 81: 
 82: # Change iteration
 83: az boards work-item update \
 84:   --id {work-item-id} \
 85:   --iteration "{ProjectName}\\Sprint 5"
 86: 
 87: # Add comment/discussion
 88: az boards work-item update \
 89:   --id {work-item-id} \
 90:   --discussion "Work in progress"
 91: 
 92: # Long comment on Windows: read the body into a PowerShell variable and call
 93: # azps.ps1 instead of az.cmd, or fall back to 'az devops invoke' with --in-file.
 94: # Full guidance in references/long-comments-on-windows.md.
 95: #
 96: # PowerShell example:
 97: #   $body = Get-Content -Raw .\comment.md
 98: #   azps.ps1 boards work-item update --id 1234 --discussion $body
 99: 
100: # Update with custom fields
101: az boards work-item update \
102:   --id {work-item-id} \
103:   --fields "Priority=1" "StoryPoints=5"
104: ```
