</file>

<file path=".github/skills/mcpee-boost-mcpee-cloud/skills/azure-pricing/references/COST-ESTIMATOR.md">
  1: # Cost Estimator Reference
  2: 
  3: Formulas and patterns for converting Azure unit prices into monthly and annual cost estimates.
  4: 
  5: ## Standard Time-Based Calculations
  6: 
  7: ### Hours per Month
  8: 
  9: Azure uses **730 hours/month** as the standard billing period (365 days × 24 hours / 12 months).
 10: 
 11: ```
 12: Monthly Cost = Unit Price per Hour × 730
 13: Annual Cost  = Monthly Cost × 12
 14: ```
 15: 
 16: ### Common Multipliers
 17: 
 18: | Period | Hours | Calculation |
 19: |--------|-------|-------------|
 20: | 1 Hour | 1 | Unit price |
 21: | 1 Day | 24 | Unit price × 24 |
 22: | 1 Week | 168 | Unit price × 168 |
 23: | 1 Month | 730 | Unit price × 730 |
 24: | 1 Year | 8,760 | Unit price × 8,760 |
 25: 
 26: ## Service-Specific Formulas
 27: 
 28: ### Virtual Machines (Compute)
 29: 
 30: ```
 31: Monthly Cost = hourly price × 730
 32: ```
 33: 
 34: For VMs that run only business hours (8h/day, 22 days/month):
 35: ```
 36: Monthly Cost = hourly price × 176
 37: ```
 38: 
 39: ### Azure Functions
 40: 
 41: ```
 42: Execution Cost = price per execution × number of executions
 43: Compute Cost   = price per GB-s × (memory in GB × execution time in seconds × number of executions)
 44: Total Monthly  = Execution Cost + Compute Cost
 45: ```
 46: 
 47: Free grant: 1M executions and 400,000 GB-s per month.
 48: 
 49: ### Azure Blob Storage
 50: 
 51: ```
 52: Storage Cost   = price per GB × storage in GB
 53: Transaction Cost = price per 10,000 ops × (operations / 10,000)
 54: Egress Cost    = price per GB × egress in GB
 55: Total Monthly  = Storage Cost + Transaction Cost + Egress Cost
 56: ```
 57: 
 58: ### Azure Cosmos DB
 59: 
 60: #### Provisioned Throughput
 61: ```
 62: Monthly Cost = (RU/s / 100) × price per 100 RU/s × 730
 63: ```
 64: 
 65: #### Serverless
 66: ```
 67: Monthly Cost = (total RUs consumed / 1,000,000) × price per 1M RUs
 68: ```
 69: 
 70: ### Azure SQL Database
 71: 
 72: #### DTU Model
 73: ```
 74: Monthly Cost = price per DTU × DTUs × 730
 75: ```
 76: 
 77: #### vCore Model
 78: ```
 79: Monthly Cost = vCore price × vCores × 730  +  storage price per GB × storage GB
 80: ```
 81: 
 82: ### Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)
 83: 
 84: ```
 85: Monthly Cost = node VM price × 730 × number of nodes
 86: ```
 87: 
 88: Control plane is free for standard tier.
 89: 
 90: ### Azure App Service
 91: 
 92: ```
 93: Monthly Cost = plan price × 730 (for hourly-priced plans)
 94: ```
 95: 
 96: Or flat monthly price for fixed-tier plans.
 97: 
 98: ### Azure OpenAI
 99: 
100: ```
101: Monthly Cost = (input tokens / 1000) × input price per 1K tokens
102:              + (output tokens / 1000) × output price per 1K tokens
103: ```
104: 
105: ## Reservation vs. Pay-As-You-Go Comparison
106: 
107: When presenting pricing options, always show the comparison:
108: 
109: ```
110: | Pricing Model | Monthly Cost | Annual Cost | Savings vs. PAYG |
111: |---------------|-------------|-------------|------------------|
112: | Pay-As-You-Go | $X | $Y | — |
113: | 1-Year Reserved | $A | $B | Z% |
114: | 3-Year Reserved | $C | $D | W% |
115: | Savings Plan (1yr) | $E | $F | V% |
116: | Savings Plan (3yr) | $G | $H | U% |
117: | Spot (if available) | $I | N/A | T% |
118: ```
119: 
120: Savings percentage formula:
121: ```
122: Savings % = ((PAYG Price - Reserved Price) / PAYG Price) × 100
123: ```
124: 
125: ## Cost Summary Table Template
126: 
127: Always present results in this format:
128: 
129: ```markdown
130: | Service | SKU | Region | Unit Price | Unit | Monthly Est. | Annual Est. |
131: |---------|-----|--------|-----------|------|-------------|-------------|
132: | Virtual Machines | Standard_D4s_v5 | East US | $0.192/hr | 1 Hour | $140.16 | $1,681.92 |
133: ```
134: 
135: ## Tips
136: 
137: - Always clarify the **usage pattern** before estimating (24/7 vs. business hours vs. sporadic).
138: - For **storage**, ask about expected data volume and access patterns.
139: - For **databases**, ask about throughput requirements (RU/s, DTUs, or vCores).
140: - For **serverless** services, ask about expected invocation count and duration.
141: - Round to 2 decimal places for display.
142: - Note that prices are in **USD** unless otherwise specified.
</file>

