377: 
378: ```text
379: edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;html=1;endArrow=ERmany;startArrow=ERmandOne;endFill=1;startFill=1;
380: ```
381: 
382: ### UML Inheritance Arrow (hollow triangle)
383: 
384: ```text
385: edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=0;
386: ```
387: 
388: ### UML Composition (filled diamond)
389: 
390: ```text
391: edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;startArrow=diamond;startFill=1;endArrow=none;
392: ```
393: 
394: ### UML Aggregation (open diamond)
395: 
396: ```text
397: edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;startArrow=diamond;startFill=0;endArrow=none;
398: ```
399: 
400: ### UML Dependency (dashed arrow)
401: 
402: ```text
403: edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;dashed=1;html=1;endArrow=open;endFill=0;
404: ```
405: 
406: ### Invisible connector (for alignment)
407: 
408: ```text
409: edgeStyle=none;strokeColor=none;endArrow=none;
410: ```
</file>

<file path=".github/skills/mcpee-boost-mcpee-cloud/skills/draw-io-diagram-generator/scripts/README.md">
  1: # draw-io Scripts
  2: 
  3: Utility scripts for working with `.drawio` diagram files in the cxp-bu-order-ms project.
  4: 
  5: ## Requirements
  6: 
  7: - Python 3.8+
  8: - No external dependencies (uses standard library only: `xml.etree.ElementTree`, `argparse`, `json`, `sys`, `pathlib`)
  9: 
 10: ## Scripts
 11: 
 12: ### `validate-drawio.py`
 13: 
 14: Validates the XML structure of a `.drawio` file against required constraints.
 15: 
 16: **Usage**
 17: 
 18: ```bash
 19: python scripts/validate-drawio.py <path-to-diagram.drawio>
 20: ```
 21: 
 22: **Examples**
 23: 
 24: ```bash
 25: # Validate a single file
 26: python scripts/validate-drawio.py docs/architecture.drawio
 27: 
 28: # Validate all drawio files in a directory
 29: for f in docs/**/*.drawio; do python scripts/validate-drawio.py "$f"; done
 30: ```
 31: 
 32: **Checks performed**
 33: 
 34: | Check | Description |
 35: |-------|-------------|
 36: | Root cells | Verifies id="0" and id="1" cells are present in every diagram page |
 37: | Unique IDs | All `mxCell` id values are unique within a diagram |
 38: | Edge connectivity | Every edge has valid `source` and `target` attributes pointing to existing cells |
 39: | Geometry | Every vertex cell has an `mxGeometry` child element |
 40: | Parent chain | Every cell's `parent` attribute references an existing cell id |
 41: | XML well-formedness | File is valid XML |
 42: 
 43: **Exit codes**
 44: 
 45: - `0` — Validation passed
 46: - `1` — One or more validation errors found (errors printed to stdout)
 47: 
 48: ---
 49: 
 50: ### `add-shape.py`
 51: 
 52: Adds a new shape (vertex cell) to an existing `.drawio` diagram file.
 53: 
 54: **Usage**
 55: 
 56: ```bash
 57: python scripts/add-shape.py <diagram.drawio> <label> <x> <y> [options]
 58: ```
 59: 
 60: **Arguments**
 61: 
 62: | Argument | Required | Description |
 63: |----------|----------|-------------|
 64: | `diagram` | Yes | Path to the `.drawio` file |
 65: | `label` | Yes | Text label for the new shape |
 66: | `x` | Yes | X coordinate (pixels from top-left) |
 67: | `y` | Yes | Y coordinate (pixels from top-left) |
 68: 
 69: **Options**
 70: 
 71: | Option | Default | Description |
 72: |--------|---------|-------------|
 73: | `--width` | `120` | Shape width in pixels |
 74: | `--height` | `60` | Shape height in pixels |
 75: | `--style` | `"rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;"` | draw.io style string |
 76: | `--diagram-index` | `0` | Index of the diagram page (0-based) |
 77: | `--dry-run` | false | Print the new cell XML without modifying the file |
 78: 
 79: **Examples**
 80: 
 81: ```bash
 82: # Add a basic rounded box
 83: python scripts/add-shape.py docs/flowchart.drawio "New Step" 400 300
 84: 
 85: # Add a custom styled shape
 86: python scripts/add-shape.py docs/flowchart.drawio "Decision" 400 400 \
 87:   --width 160 --height 80 \
 88:   --style "rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;"
 89: 
 90: # Preview without writing
 91: python scripts/add-shape.py docs/architecture.drawio "Service X" 600 200 --dry-run
 92: ```
 93: 
 94: **Output**
 95: 
 96: Prints the new cell id on success:
 97: ```
 98: Added shape id="auto_abc123" to page 0 of docs/flowchart.drawio
 99: ```
100: 
101: ---
102: 
103: ## Common Workflows
104: 
105: ### Validate before committing
106: 
107: ```bash
108: # Validate all diagrams
109: find . -name "*.drawio" -not -path "*/node_modules/*" | \
110:   xargs -I{} python scripts/validate-drawio.py {}
111: ```
112: 
113: ### Quickly add a placeholder node
114: 
115: ```bash
116: python scripts/add-shape.py docs/architecture.drawio "TODO: Service" 800 400 \
117:   --style "rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;"
118: ```
119: 
120: ### Check a template is valid
121: 
122: ```bash
123: python scripts/validate-drawio.py .github/skills/draw-io-diagram-generator/templates/flowchart.drawio
124: ```
</file>

<file path=".github/skills/mcpee-boost-mcpee-cloud/skills/draw-io-diagram-generator/SKILL.md">
  1: ---
  2: name: draw-io-diagram-generator
  3: description: Use when creating, editing, or generating draw.io diagram files (.drawio, .drawio.svg, .drawio.png). Covers mxGraph XML authoring, shape libraries, style strings, flowcharts, system architecture, sequence diagrams, ER diagrams, UML class diagrams, network topology, layout strategy, the hediet.vscode-drawio VS Code extension, and the full agent workflow from request to a ready-to-open file.
  4: ---
  5: 
  6: # Draw.io Diagram Generator
  7: 
  8: This skill enables you to generate, edit, and validate draw.io (`.drawio`) diagram files with
  9: correct mxGraph XML structure. All generated files open immediately in the
 10: [Draw.io VS Code extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=hediet.vscode-drawio)
 11: (`hediet.vscode-drawio`) without any manual fixes required. You can also open the files in the draw.io web app or desktop app if you prefer.
 12: 
 13: ---
 14: 
 15: ## 1. When to Use This Skill
 16: 
 17: **Trigger phrases (load this skill when you see these)**
 18: 
 19: - "create a diagram", "draw a flowchart", "generate an architecture diagram"
 20: - "design a sequence diagram", "make a UML class diagram", "build an ER diagram"
 21: - "add a .drawio file", "update the diagram", "visualise the flow"
 22: - "document the architecture", "show the data model", "diagram the service interactions"
 23: - Any request to produce or modify a `.drawio`, `.drawio.svg`, or `.drawio.png` file
 24: 
 25: **Supported diagram types**
 26: 
 27: | Diagram Type | Template Available | Description |
 28: |---|---|---|
 29: | Flowchart | `assets/templates/flowchart.drawio` | Process flows with decisions and branches |
 30: | System Architecture | `assets/templates/architecture.drawio` | Multi-tier / layered service architecture |
 31: | Sequence Diagram | `assets/templates/sequence.drawio` | Actor lifelines and timed message flows |
 32: | ER Diagram | `assets/templates/er-diagram.drawio` | Database tables with relationships |
 33: | UML Class Diagram | `assets/templates/uml-class.drawio` | Classes, interfaces, enums, relationships |
 34: | Network Topology | (use shape library) | Routers, servers, firewalls, subnets |
 35: | BPMN Workflow | (use shape library) | Business process events, tasks, gateways |
 36: | Mind Map | (manual) | Central topic with radiating branches |
 37: 
 38: ---
 39: 
 40: ## 2. Prerequisites
 41: 
 42: - If running with VS Code integration enabled, Install the drawio extension: **draw.io VS Code extension** — `hediet.vscode-drawio` (extension id). Install with:
 43:   ```
 44:   ext install hediet.vscode-drawio
 45:   ```
 46: - **Supported file extensions**: `.drawio`, `.drawio.svg`, `.drawio.png`
 47: - **Python 3.8+** (optional) — for the validation and shape-insertion scripts in `scripts/`
 48: 
 49: ---
 50: 
 51: ## 3. Step-by-Step Agent Workflow
 52: 
 53: Follow these steps in order for every diagram generation task.
 54: 
 55: ### Step 1 — Understand the Request
 56: 
 57: Ask or infer:
 58: 1. **Diagram type** — What kind of diagram? (flowchart, architecture, UML, ER, sequence, network...)
 59: 2. **Entities / actors** — What are the main components, actors, classes, or tables?
 60: 3. **Relationships** — How are they connected? What direction? What cardinality?
 61: 4. **Output path** — Where should the `.drawio` file be saved?
 62: 5. **Existing file** — Are we creating new or editing an existing file?
 63: 
 64: If the request is ambiguous, infer the most sensible diagram type from context (e.g. "show the tables" → ER diagram, "show how the API call flows" → sequence diagram).
 65: 
 66: ### Step 2 — Select a Template or Start Fresh
 67: 
 68: - **Use a template** when the diagram type matches one in `assets/templates/`. Copy the template structure and replace placeholder values.
 69: - **Start fresh** for novel layouts. Begin with the minimal valid skeleton:
 70: 
 71: ```xml
 72: <!-- Set modified="" to the current ISO 8601 timestamp when generating a new file -->
 73: <mxfile host="Electron" modified="" version="26.0.0">
 74:   <diagram id="page-1" name="Page-1">
 75:     <mxGraphModel dx="1422" dy="762" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1"
 76:                   tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1"
 77:                   page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="827"
 78:                   math="0" shadow="0">
 79:       <root>
 80:         <mxCell id="0" />
 81:         <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
 82:         <!-- Your cells go here -->
 83:       </root>
 84:     </mxGraphModel>
 85:   </diagram>
 86: </mxfile>
 87: ```
 88: 
 89: > **Rule**: ids `0` and `1` are ALWAYS required and must be the first two cells. Never reuse them.
 90: 
 91: ### Step 3 — Plan the Layout
 92: 
 93: Before generating XML, sketch the logical placement:
 94: - Organise into **rows** or **tiers** (use swimlanes for layers)
 95: - **Horizontal spacing**: 40–60px between same-row shapes
 96: - **Vertical spacing**: 80–120px between tier rows
 97: - Standard shape size: `120x60` px for process boxes, `160x80` px for swimlanes
 98: - Default canvas: A4 landscape = `1169 x 827` px
 99: 
100: ### Step 4 — Generate the mxGraph XML
101: 
102: **Vertex cell** (every shape):
103: ```xml
104: <mxCell id="unique-id" value="Label"
105:         style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;"
106:         vertex="1" parent="1">
107:   <mxGeometry x="100" y="100" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
108: </mxCell>
109: ```
110: 
111: **Edge cell** (every connector):
112: ```xml
113: <mxCell id="edge-id" value="Label (optional)"
114:         style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;"
115:         edge="1" source="source-id" target="target-id" parent="1">
116:   <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
117: </mxCell>
118: ```
119: 
120: **Critical rules**:
121: - Every cell id must be **globally unique** within the file
122: - Every vertex must have an `mxGeometry` child with `x`, `y`, `width`, `height`, `as="geometry"`
123: - Every edge must have `source` and `target` matching existing vertex ids — **exception**: floating edges (e.g. sequence diagram lifelines) use `sourcePoint`/`targetPoint` inside `<mxGeometry>` instead; see §4 Sequence Diagram
124: - Every cell's `parent` must reference an existing cell id
125: - Use `html=1` in style when the label contains HTML (`<b>`, `<i>`, `<br>`)
126: - Escape XML special characters in labels: `&` => `&amp;`, `<` => `&lt;`, `>` => `&gt;`
127: 
128: ### Step 5 — Apply Correct Styles
129: 
130: Use the standard semantic color palette for consistency:
131: 
132: | Purpose | fillColor | strokeColor |
133: |---|---|---|
134: | Primary / Info | `#dae8fc` | `#6c8ebf` |
135: | Success / Start | `#d5e8d4` | `#82b366` |
136: | Warning / Decision | `#fff2cc` | `#d6b656` |
137: | Error / End | `#f8cecc` | `#b85450` |
138: | Neutral | `#f5f5f5` | `#666666` |
139: | External / Partner | `#e1d5e7` | `#9673a6` |
140: 
141: Common style strings by diagram type:
142: 
143: ```
144: # Rounded process box (flowchart)
145: rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;
146: 
147: # Decision diamond
148: rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;
149: 
150: # Start/End terminal
151: ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;
152: 
153: # Database cylinder
154: shape=mxgraph.flowchart.database;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;
155: 
156: # Swimlane container (tier)
157: swimlane;startSize=30;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontStyle=1;
158: 
159: # UML class box
160: swimlane;fontStyle=1;align=center;startSize=40;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;
161: 
162: # Interface / stereotype box
163: swimlane;fontStyle=3;align=center;startSize=40;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;
164: 
165: # ER table container
166: shape=table;startSize=30;container=1;collapsible=1;childLayout=tableLayout;
167: 
168: # Orthogonal connector
169: edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;
170: 
171: # ER relationship (crow's foot)
172: edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;html=1;endArrow=ERmany;startArrow=ERone;
173: ```
174: 
175: > See `references/style-reference.md` for the complete style key catalog and `references/shape-libraries.md` for all shape library names.
176: 
177: ### Step 6 — Save and Validate
178: 
179: 1. **Write the file** to the requested path with `.drawio` extension
180: 2. **Run the validator** (optional but recommended):
181:    ```bash
182:    python .github/skills/draw-io-diagram-generator/scripts/validate-drawio.py <path-to-file.drawio>
183:    ```
184: 3. **Tell the user** how to open the file:
185:    > "Open `<filename>` in VS Code — it will render automatically with the draw.io extension. You can use draw.io's web app or desktop app as well if you prefer."
186: 4. **Provide a brief description** of what is in the diagram so the user knows what to expect.
187: 
188: ---
189: 
190: ## 4. Diagram-Type Recipes
191: 
192: ### Flowchart
193: 
194: Key elements: Start (ellipse) => Process (rounded rectangle) => Decision (diamond) => End (ellipse)
195: 
196: ```xml
197: <!-- Start node -->
198: <mxCell id="start" value="Start"
199:         style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;"
200:         vertex="1" parent="1">
201:   <mxGeometry x="500" y="80" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
202: </mxCell>
203: 
204: <!-- Process -->
205: <mxCell id="p1" value="Process Step"
206:         style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;"
207:         vertex="1" parent="1">
208:   <mxGeometry x="500" y="200" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
209: </mxCell>
210: 
211: <!-- Decision -->
212: <mxCell id="d1" value="Condition?"
213:         style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;"
214:         vertex="1" parent="1">
215:   <mxGeometry x="460" y="320" width="200" height="100" as="geometry" />
216: </mxCell>
217: 
218: <!-- Arrow: start to p1 -->
219: <mxCell id="e1" value=""
220:         style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;"
221:         edge="1" source="start" target="p1" parent="1">
222:   <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
223: </mxCell>
224: ```
225: 
226: ### Architecture Diagram (3-tier)
227: 
228: Use **swimlane containers** for each tier. All service boxes are children of their swimlane.
229: 
230: ```xml
231: <!-- Tier swimlane -->
232: <mxCell id="tier1" value="Client Layer"
233:         style="swimlane;startSize=30;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontStyle=1;"
234:         vertex="1" parent="1">
235:   <mxGeometry x="60" y="100" width="1050" height="130" as="geometry" />
236: </mxCell>
237: 
238: <!-- Service inside tier (parent="tier1", coords are relative to tier) -->
239: <mxCell id="webapp" value="Web App"
240:         style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;"
241:         vertex="1" parent="tier1">
242:   <mxGeometry x="80" y="40" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
243: </mxCell>
244: ```
245: 
246: > Connectors between tiers use absolute coordinates with `parent="1"`.
247: 
248: ### Sequence Diagram
249: 
250: Key elements: Actors (top), Lifelines (dashed vertical lines), Activation boxes, Message arrows.
251: 
252: - Lifelines: `edge="1"` with `endArrow=none` and `dashed=1`, no source/target — use `sourcePoint`/`targetPoint` in geometry
253: - Synchronous message: `endArrow=block;endFill=1`
254: - Return message: `endArrow=open;endFill=0;dashed=1`
255: - Self-call: loop the edge via two Array points to the right and back
256: 
257: **Minimal XML snippet:**
258: 
259: ```xml
260: <!-- Actor (stick figure) -->
261: <mxCell id="actorA" value="Client"
262:         style="shape=mxgraph.uml.actor;pointerEvents=1;dashed=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;"
263:         vertex="1" parent="1">
264:   <mxGeometry x="110" y="80" width="60" height="80" as="geometry" />
265: </mxCell>
266: 
267: <!-- Service box -->
268: <mxCell id="actorB" value="API Server"
269:         style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;"
270:         vertex="1" parent="1">
271:   <mxGeometry x="480" y="100" width="160" height="60" as="geometry" />
272: </mxCell>
273: 
274: <!-- Lifeline — floating edge: uses sourcePoint/targetPoint, NOT source/target attributes -->
275: <mxCell id="lifA" value=""
276:         style="edgeStyle=none;dashed=1;endArrow=none;"
277:         edge="1" parent="1">
278:   <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
279:     <mxPoint x="140" y="160" as="sourcePoint" />
280:     <mxPoint x="140" y="700" as="targetPoint" />
281:   </mxGeometry>
282: </mxCell>
283: 
284: <!-- Activation box (thin rectangle on lifeline) -->
285: <mxCell id="actA1" value=""
286:         style="fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;"
287:         vertex="1" parent="1">
288:   <mxGeometry x="130" y="220" width="20" height="180" as="geometry" />
289: </mxCell>
290: 
291: <!-- Synchronous message -->
292: <mxCell id="msg1" value="POST /orders"
293:         style="edgeStyle=elbowEdgeStyle;elbow=vertical;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;"
294:         edge="1" source="actA1" target="actorB" parent="1">
295:   <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
296: </mxCell>
297: 
298: <!-- Return message (dashed) -->
299: <mxCell id="msg2" value="201 Created"
300:         style="edgeStyle=elbowEdgeStyle;elbow=vertical;dashed=1;html=1;endArrow=open;endFill=0;"
301:         edge="1" source="actorB" target="actA1" parent="1">
302:   <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
303: </mxCell>
304: ```
305: 
306: > **Note:** Lifelines are floating edges that use `sourcePoint`/`targetPoint` in `<mxGeometry>` instead of `source`/`target` attributes. This is the standard draw.io pattern for sequence diagrams.
307: 
308: ### ER Diagram
309: 
310: Use `shape=table` containers with `childLayout=tableLayout`. Rows are `shape=tableRow` cells with `portConstraint=eastwest`. Columns inside each row are `shape=partialRectangle`.
311: 
312: Relationship arrows use `edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle`:
313: - One-to-One: `startArrow=ERone;endArrow=ERone`
314: - One-to-Many: `startArrow=ERone;endArrow=ERmany`
315: - Many-to-Many: `startArrow=ERmany;endArrow=ERmany`
316: - Mandatory: `ERmandOne`, Optional: `ERzeroToOne`
317: 
318: ### UML Class Diagram
319: 
320: Class boxes are swimlane containers. Attributes and methods are plain text cells. Dividers are zero-height swimlane children.
321: 
322: Arrow styles by relationship type:
323: 
324: | Relationship | Style String |
325: |---|---|
326: | Inheritance (extends) | `edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=0;` |
327: | Realization (implements) | `edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;dashed=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=0;` |
328: | Composition | `edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;startArrow=diamond;startFill=1;endArrow=none;` |
329: | Aggregation | `edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;startArrow=diamond;startFill=0;endArrow=none;` |
330: | Dependency | `edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;dashed=1;html=1;endArrow=open;endFill=0;` |
331: | Association | `edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;endArrow=open;endFill=0;` |
332: 
333: ---
334: 
335: ## 5. Multi-Page Diagrams
336: 
337: Add multiple `<diagram>` elements for complex systems:
338: 
339: ```xml
340: <mxfile host="Electron" version="26.0.0">
341:   <diagram id="overview" name="Overview">
342:     <!-- overview mxGraphModel -->
343:   </diagram>
344:   <diagram id="detail" name="Detail View">
345:     <!-- detail mxGraphModel -->
346:   </diagram>
347: </mxfile>
348: ```
349: 
350: Each page has its own independent cell id namespace. The same id value can appear in different pages without conflict.
351: 
352: ---
353: 
354: ## 6. Editing Existing Diagrams
355: 
356: When modifying an existing `.drawio` file:
357: 
358: 1. **Read** the file first to understand existing cell ids, positions, and parent hierarchy
359: 2. **Identify the target diagram page** — by index or `name` attribute
360: 3. **Assign new unique ids** that do not collide with existing ids
361: 4. **Respect the container hierarchy** — children of a swimlane use coordinates relative to their parent
362: 5. **Verify edges** — after repositioning nodes, confirm edge source/target ids remain valid
363: 
364: Use `scripts/add-shape.py` to safely add a single shape without editing raw XML:
365: ```bash
366: python .github/skills/draw-io-diagram-generator/scripts/add-shape.py docs/arch.drawio "New Service" 700 380
367: ```
368: 
369: ---
370: 
371: ## 7. Best Practices
372: 
373: **Layout**
374: - Align shapes to the 10px grid (all coordinates divisible by 10)
375: - Group related shapes inside swimlane containers
376: - One diagram topic per page; use multi-page files for complex systems
377: - Aim for 40 or fewer cells per page for readability
378: 
379: **Labels**
380: - Add a title text cell (`text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1`) at top of every page
381: - Always set `whiteSpace=wrap;html=1` on vertex shapes
382: - Keep labels concise — 3 words or fewer per shape where possible
383: 
384: **Style consistency**
385: - Use the semantic color palette from Section 3 Step 5 consistently across a project
386: - Prefer `edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle` for clean right-angle connectors
387: - Do not inline arbitrary HTML in labels unless necessary
388: 
389: **File naming**
390: - Use kebab-case: `order-service-flow.drawio`, `database-schema.drawio`
391: - Place diagrams alongside the code they document: `docs/` or `architecture/`
392: 
393: ---
394: 
395: ## 8. Troubleshooting
396: 
397: | Problem | Likely Cause | Fix |
398: |---|---|---|
399: | File opens blank in VS Code | Missing id=0 or id=1 cell | Add both root cells before any other cells |
400: | Shape at wrong position | Child inside container — coords are relative | Check `parent`; adjust x/y relative to container |
401: | Edge not visible | source or target id does not match any vertex | Verify both ids exist exactly as written |
402: | Diagram shows "Compressed" | mxGraphModel is base64-encoded | Open in draw.io web, File > Export > XML (uncompressed) |
403: | Shape style not rendering | Typo in shape= name | Check `references/shape-libraries.md` for exact style string |
404: | Label shows escaped HTML | html=0 on a cell with HTML label | Add `html=1;` to the cell style |
405: | Container children overlap container edge | Container height too small | Increase container height in mxGeometry |
406: 
407: ---
408: 
409: ## 9. Validation Checklist
410: 
411: Before delivering any generated `.drawio` file, verify:
412: 
413: - [ ] File starts with `<mxfile>` root element
414: - [ ] Every `<diagram>` has a non-empty `id` attribute
415: - [ ] `<mxCell id="0" />` is the first cell in every diagram
416: - [ ] `<mxCell id="1" parent="0" />` is the second cell in every diagram
417: - [ ] All cell `id` values are unique within each diagram
418: - [ ] Every vertex cell has `vertex="1"` and a child `<mxGeometry as="geometry">`
419: - [ ] Every edge cell has `edge="1"` and either: (a) `source`/`target` pointing to existing vertex ids, or (b) `<mxPoint as="sourcePoint">` and `<mxPoint as="targetPoint">` in its `<mxGeometry>` (floating edge — used for sequence diagram lifelines)
420: - [ ] Every cell (except id=0) has a `parent` pointing to an existing id
421: - [ ] `html=1` is in the style for any label containing HTML tags
422: - [ ] XML is well-formed (no unclosed tags, no unescaped `&`, `<`, `>` in attribute values)
423: - [ ] A title label cell exists at the top of each page
424: 
425: Run the automated validator:
426: ```bash
427: python .github/skills/draw-io-diagram-generator/scripts/validate-drawio.py <file.drawio>
428: ```
429: 
430: ---
431: 
432: ## 10. Output Format
433: 
434: When delivering a diagram, always provide:
435: 
436: 1. **The `.drawio` file** written to the requested path
437: 2. **A one-sentence summary** of what the diagram shows
438: 3. **How to open it**:
439:    > "Open `<filename>` in VS Code — the draw.io extension will render it automatically. Or you can open it in the draw.io web app or desktop app if you prefer."
440: 4. **How to edit it** (if the user is likely to customise):
441:    > "Click any shape to select it. Double-click to edit the label. Drag to reposition."
442: 5. **Validation status** — whether the validator script was run and passed
443: 
444: ---
445: 
446: ## 11. References
447: 
448: All companion files are in `.github/skills/draw-io-diagram-generator/`:
449: 
450: | File | Contents |
451: |---|---|
452: | `references/drawio-xml-schema.md` | Complete mxfile / mxGraphModel / mxCell attribute reference, coordinate system, reserved cells, validation rules |
453: | `references/style-reference.md` | All style keys with allowed values, vertex and edge style keys, shape catalog, semantic color palette |
454: | `references/shape-libraries.md` | All shape library categories (General, Flowchart, UML, ER, Network, BPMN, Mockup, K8s) with style strings |
455: | `assets/templates/flowchart.drawio` | Ready-to-use flowchart template |
456: | `assets/templates/architecture.drawio` | 4-tier system architecture template |
457: | `assets/templates/sequence.drawio` | 3-actor sequence diagram template |
458: | `assets/templates/er-diagram.drawio` | 3-table ER diagram with crow's foot relationships |
459: | `assets/templates/uml-class.drawio` | Interface + 2 classes + enum with relationship arrows |
460: | `scripts/validate-drawio.py` | Python script to validate XML structure of any .drawio file |
461: | `scripts/add-shape.py` | Python CLI to add a new shape to an existing diagram |
462: | `scripts/README.md` | How to use the scripts with examples |
</file>

