  1: ---
  2: name: 'design-patterns-library'
  3: description: 'Librería completa de design patterns basada en Material Design, patrones ARIA, WAI-ARIA y patrones UX probados. Proporciona implementaciones de patrones testeadas, accesibles y reutilizables.'
  4: ---
  5: 
  6: # Skill de Librería de Design Patterns
  7: 
  8: Este skill proporciona una base de **design patterns probados y testeados** de fuentes líderes de la industria.
  9: 
 10: ## Fundamentos y Referencias
 11: 
 12: ### Estándares Oficiales
 13: - **ARIA Authoring Practices**: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/
 14: - **Material Design System**: https://material.io/design
 15: - **Apple Human Interface Guidelines**: https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines
 16: - **WCAG 2.1 Guidelines**: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/quickref/
 17: - **WAI-ARIA 1.2**: https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/
 18: 
 19: ### Fuentes de Patrones Probados
 20: - Shopify Polaris: https://polaris.shopify.com/
 21: - Atlassian Design System: https://atlassian.design/
 22: - IBM Carbon Design System: https://www.carbondesignsystem.com/
 23: - GitHub Primer: https://primer.style/
 24: - Figma Design Tokens: https://www.figma.com/resource-library/design-tokens/
 25: 
 26: ## Categorías de Patrones
 27: 
 28: ### 1. Patrones de Navegación
 29: 
 30: #### Patrón Tabs (ARIA Tab)
 31: ```typescript
 32: // From: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/tabs/
 33: 
 34: interface TabProps {
 35:   label: string;
 36:   id: string;
 37:   isSelected: boolean;
 38:   onChange: () => void;
 39: }
 40: 
 41: export const Tab: React.FC<TabProps> = ({ label, id, isSelected, onChange }) => (
 42:   <button
 43:     role="tab"
 44:     aria-selected={isSelected}
 45:     aria-controls={`tabpanel-${id}`}
 46:     id={`tab-${id}`}
 47:     onClick={onChange}
 48:     className={isSelected ? 'tab--active' : 'tab'}
 49:   >
 50:     {label}
 51:   </button>
 52: );
 53: 
 54: export const TabPanel: React.FC<{ id: string; children: React.ReactNode }> = ({ id, children }) => (
 55:   <div
 56:     role="tabpanel"
 57:     id={`tabpanel-${id}`}
 58:     aria-labelledby={`tab-${id}`}
 59:     className="tab-panel"
 60:   >
 61:     {children}
 62:   </div>
 63: );
 64: ```
 65: 
 66: **Checklist del Patrón:**
 67: - [ ] Navegación por teclado: teclas de flecha entre tabs
 68: - [ ] Primer tab enfocado por defecto (teclas Home/End)
 69: - [ ] `role="tab"` en los botones de tab
 70: - [ ] `role="tabpanel"` en los paneles
 71: - [ ] `aria-selected` en el tab activo
 72: - [ ] `aria-controls` enlazando tab al panel
 73: - [ ] `aria-labelledby` enlazando panel al tab
 74: - [ ] El contenido del tab sigue al tab (orden DOM)
 75: 
 76: #### Navegación Breadcrumb
 77: ```typescript
 78: // From: Material Design Navigation
 79: 
 80: export const Breadcrumbs: React.FC<{ items: BreadcrumbItem[] }> = ({ items }) => (
 81:   <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
 82:     <ol className="breadcrumbs">
 83:       {items.map((item, index) => (
 84:         <li key={item.id}>
 85:           <a href={item.href} aria-current={index === items.length - 1 ? 'page' : undefined}>
 86:             {item.label}
 87:           </a>
 88:           {index < items.length - 1 && <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>}
 89:         </li>
 90:       ))}
 91:     </ol>
 92:   </nav>
 93: );
 94: ```
 95: 
 96: ### 2. Patrones de Formulario
 97: 
 98: #### Patrón de Input Validado (ARIA Live Regions)
 99: ```typescript
100: // From: ARIA APG - Form Patterns
101: 
102: interface InputProps {
103:   label: string;
104:   error?: string;
105:   required?: boolean;
106: }
107: 
108: export const Input: React.FC<InputProps> = ({ label, error, required }) => {
109:   const inputId = useId();
110:   const errorId = useId();
111: 
112:   return (
113:     <div className="form-group">
114:       <label htmlFor={inputId}>
115:         {label}
116:         {required && <span aria-label="required">*</span>}
117:       </label>
118:       <input
119:         id={inputId}
120:         type="text"
121:         aria-invalid={!!error}
122:         aria-describedby={error ? errorId : undefined}
123:         required={required}
124:         className={error ? 'input--error' : 'input'}
125:       />
126:       {error && (
127:         <div id={errorId} role="alert" className="error-message">
128:           {error}
129:         </div>
130:       )}
131:     </div>
132:   );
133: };
134: ```
135: 
136: **Checklist del Patrón:**
137: - [ ] Etiqueta asociada con `htmlFor`
138: - [ ] `aria-invalid` cuando hay error
139: - [ ] `aria-describedby` enlazando al mensaje de error
140: - [ ] El mensaje de error tiene `role="alert"`
141: - [ ] Indicador de requerido etiquetado
142: - [ ] Touch target >= 44x44px
143: - [ ] Mensajes de error claros
144: - [ ] Texto de ayuda con `aria-describedby`
145: 
146: #### Combobox / Autocomplete (ARIA Combobox)
147: ```typescript
148: // From: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/combobox/
149: 
150: // Complex pattern with:
151: - [ ] Role="combobox" on input
152: - [ ] Role="listbox" on dropdown
153: - [ ] Role="option" on items
154: - [ ] aria-expanded on trigger
155: - [ ] aria-haspopup="listbox"
156: - [ ] aria-owns linking combobox to listbox
157: - [ ] aria-activedescendant for focus management
158: - [ ] Keyboard support: ArrowDown, ArrowUp, Enter, Escape
159: - [ ] Filtering/search logic
160: - [ ] Touch accessible
161: ```
162: 
163: ### 3. Patrones de Disclosure/Accordion
164: 
165: #### Patrón Accordion
166: ```typescript
167: // From: Material Design & ARIA APG
168: 
169: interface AccordionItemProps {
170:   title: string;
171:   children: React.ReactNode;
172:   defaultOpen?: boolean;
173: }
174: 
175: export const AccordionItem: React.FC<AccordionItemProps> = ({ title, children, defaultOpen }) => {
176:   const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(defaultOpen ?? false);
177:   const headingId = useId();
178: 
179:   return (
180:     <div className="accordion-item">
181:       <h3 id={headingId} className="accordion-header">
182:         <button
183:           className="accordion-trigger"
184:           aria-expanded={isOpen}
185:           aria-controls={`panel-${headingId}`}
186:           onClick={() => setIsOpen(!isOpen)}
187:         >
188:           <span>{title}</span>
189:           <svg className="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true">
190:             <use href="#icon-chevron" />
191:           </svg>
192:         </button>
193:       </h3>
194:       {isOpen && (
195:         <div id={`panel-${headingId}`} className="accordion-panel">
196:           {children}
197:         </div>
198:       )}
199:     </div>
200:   );
201: };
202: ```
203: 
204: **Checklist del Patrón:**
205: - [ ] Botón con `aria-expanded`
206: - [ ] `aria-controls` en el botón
207: - [ ] El icono es `aria-hidden="true"`
208: - [ ] Soporte de teclado: Enter/Space para alternar
209: - [ ] Contenido oculto cuando está cerrado (DOM o display:none)
210: - [ ] Transiciones suaves
211: - [ ] Solo un panel abierto (opcional - depende del diseño)
212: 
213: ### 4. Patrones de Diálogo/Modal
214: 
215: #### Diálogo Modal (ARIA Dialog)
216: ```typescript
217: // From: ARIA APG - Dialog Pattern
218: 
219: interface ModalProps {
220:   isOpen: boolean;
221:   onClose: () => void;
222:   title: string;
223:   children: React.ReactNode;
224: }
225: 
226: export const Modal: React.FC<ModalProps> = ({ isOpen, onClose, title, children }) => {
227:   const titleId = useId();
228: 
229:   useEffect(() => {
230:     if (isOpen) {
231:       document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
232:       // Trap focus
233:       return () => {
234:         document.body.style.overflow = '';
235:       };
236:     }
237:   }, [isOpen]);
238: 
239:   if (!isOpen) return null;
240: 
241:   return (
242:     <>
243:       {/* Backdrop */}
244:       <div
245:         className="modal-backdrop"
246:         onClick={onClose}
247:         aria-hidden="true"
248:       />
249:       {/* Dialog */}
250:       <div
251:         className="modal"
252:         role="dialog"
253:         aria-modal="true"
254:         aria-labelledby={titleId}
255:         aria-describedby="modal-description"
256:       >
257:         <div className="modal-header">
258:           <h2 id={titleId}>{title}</h2>
259:           <button
260:             onClick={onClose}
261:             aria-label="Close dialog"
262:             className="modal-close"
263:           >
264:             ×
265:           </button>
266:         </div>
267:         <div id="modal-description" className="modal-body">
268:           {children}
269:         </div>
270:       </div>
271:     </>
272:   );
273: };
274: ```
275: 
276: **Checklist del Patrón:**
277: - [ ] `role="dialog"`
278: - [ ] `aria-modal="true"`
279: - [ ] `aria-labelledby` en el título
280: - [ ] `aria-describedby` en el contenido
281: - [ ] El backdrop evita interacción detrás del modal
282: - [ ] Trampa de foco (Tab dentro del modal)
283: - [ ] Tecla Escape para cerrar
284: - [ ] Previene scroll del body
285: - [ ] Devuelve el foco al cerrar
286: - [ ] El backdrop es `aria-hidden="true"`
287: 
288: ### 5. Patrones de Notificación/Alerta
289: 
290: #### Alerta de Live Region
291: ```typescript
292: // From: WCAG 2.1 & ARIA APG
293: 
294: interface AlertProps {
295:   message: string;
296:   type: 'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'error';
297:   onDismiss?: () => void;
298: }
299: 
300: export const Alert: React.FC<AlertProps> = ({ message, type, onDismiss }) => (
301:   <div
302:     className={`alert alert--${type}`}
303:     role="alert"
304:     aria-live="polite"
305:     aria-atomic="true"
306:   >
307:     <div className="alert-content">{message}</div>
308:     {onDismiss && (
309:       <button onClick={onDismiss} aria-label="Dismiss alert" className="alert-close">
310:         ×
311:       </button>
312:     )}
313:   </div>
314: );
315: ```
316: 
317: **Pattern Checklist:**
318: - [ ] `role="alert"` for urgent notifications
319: - [ ] `aria-live="polite"` for non-urgent
320: - [ ] `aria-atomic="true"` to announce entire message
321: - [ ] Auto-dismiss after delay (optional)
322: - [ ] Keyboard dismissible
323: - [ ] Appropriate color + icon (not color alone)
324: - [ ] Contrast meets WCAG AA
325: - [ ] Positioned where users will see it
326: 
327: ### 6. Menu Patterns
328: 
329: #### Dropdown Menu
330: ```typescript
331: // From: ARIA APG - Menu Button Pattern
332: 
333: interface MenuProps {
334:   trigger: React.ReactNode;
335:   items: MenuItem[];
336: }
337: 
338: export const Menu: React.FC<MenuProps> = ({ trigger, items }) => {
339:   const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);
340:   const menuId = useId();
341: 
342:   return (
343:     <div className="menu-wrapper">
344:       <button
345:         aria-haspopup="menu"
346:         aria-expanded={isOpen}
347:         onClick={() => setIsOpen(!isOpen)}
348:       >
349:         {trigger}
350:       </button>
351:       {isOpen && (
352:         <ul
353:           id={menuId}
354:           role="menu"
355:           className="menu"
356:           onKeyDown={(e) => {
357:             if (e.key === 'Escape') setIsOpen(false);
358:           }}
359:         >
360:           {items.map((item) => (
361:             <li key={item.id} role="none">
362:               <a role="menuitem" href={item.href}>
363:                 {item.label}
364:               </a>
365:             </li>
366:           ))}
367:         </ul>
368:       )}
369:     </div>
370:   );
371: };
372: ```
373: 
374: **Pattern Checklist:**
375: - [ ] `aria-haspopup="menu"` on trigger
376: - [ ] `aria-expanded` on trigger
377: - [ ] `role="menu"` on container
378: - [ ] `role="menuitem"` on items
379: - [ ] Keyboard: Arrow keys to navigate
380: - [ ] Enter/Space to activate
381: - [ ] Escape to close
382: - [ ] Mouse click outside closes menu
383: - [ ] First item focused when opened
384: 
385: ## Layout & Grid Patterns
386: 
387: ### Responsive Layout Breakpoints (Industry Standard)
388: ```typescript
389: // From: Material Design & Web Best Practices
390: 
391: const breakpoints = {
392:   xs: 320,   // Mobile phone
393:   sm: 480,   // Mobile landscape
394:   md: 768,   // Tablet
395:   lg: 1024,  // Desktop
396:   xl: 1280,  // Large desktop
397:   xxl: 1536, // Extra large
398: };
399: 
400: const mediaQueries = {
401:   mobile: '@media (max-width: 479px)',
402:   tablet: '@media (min-width: 480px) and (max-width: 1023px)',
403:   desktop: '@media (min-width: 1024px)',
404: };
405: ```
406: 
407: ## Touch Target Size Pattern
408: 
409: ```typescript
410: // From: WCAG 2.5.5 - Target Size (Level AAA)
411: 
412: // ✅ Recommended: 48x48px (Material Design)
413: // ✅ Minimum: 44x44px (Apple, WCAG AAA)
414: // ⚠️ Minimum: 24x24px (WCAG Level AA - but larger is better)
415: 
416: const touchTargetStyles = {
417:   button: {
418:     minHeight: '44px', // Touch target size
419:     minWidth: '44px',
420:     padding: '12px 16px', // Comfortable clicking
421:   },
422:   link: {
423:     minHeight: '44px', // Clickable area
424:     padding: '8px 12px',
425:   },
426: };
427: ```
428: 
429: ## Color & Contrast Patterns
430: 
431: ```typescript
432: // From: WCAG 2.1 - Color Contrast
433: 
434: // Level AA (Minimum)
435: // - Normal text: 4.5:1 ratio
436: // - Large text (18pt+): 3:1 ratio
437: 
438: // Level AAA (Enhanced)
439: // - Normal text: 7:1 ratio
440: // - Large text: 4.5:1 ratio
441: 
442: const contrastValidator = {
443:   checkContrast: (foreground: string, background: string): boolean => {
444:     const l1 = getLuminance(foreground);
445:     const l2 = getLuminance(background);
446:     const lighter = Math.max(l1, l2);
447:     const darker = Math.min(l1, l2);
448:     const ratio = (lighter + 0.05) / (darker + 0.05);
449:     return ratio >= 4.5; // Level AA
450:   },
451: };
452: ```
453: 
454: ## Icon & Visual Indicators Pattern
455: 
456: ```typescript
457: // From: WCAG 2.1 - Use of Color
458: 
459: // ✅ Do use multiple visual indicators
460: export const ErrorInput = () => (
461:   <div className="form-group">
462:     <input aria-invalid="true" className="input--error" />
463:     {/* Icon + Text + Color */}
464:     <svg className="error-icon" aria-hidden="true">
465:       <use href="#icon-error" />
466:     </svg>
467:     <span className="error-text">This field is required</span>
468:   </div>
469: );
470: 
471: // ❌ Don't rely on color alone
472: const BadBadge = ({ type }: { type: 'success' | 'error' }) => (
473:   <span style={{ color: type === 'success' ? 'green' : 'red' }}>
474:     Status
475:   </span>
476: );
477: ```
478: 
479: ## Animation & Motion Patterns
480: 
481: ```typescript
482: // From: WCAG 2.3.3 - Animation from Interactions
483: 
484: // ✅ Respect prefers-reduced-motion
485: const transitionStyles = css`
486:   @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
487:     transition: all 300ms ease-in-out;
488:   }
489:   @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
490:     transition: none;
491:   }
492: `;
493: 
494: // ✅ Avoid animations that flash
495: // - Frequency > 3 flashes per second = risk of seizures
496: // - Avoid photosensitive triggers
497: ```
498: 
499: ## Form Validation Pattern
500: 
501: ```typescript
502: // From: ARIA APG - Form Validation
503: 
504: export const FormValidation = () => {
505:   const [errors, setErrors] = useState<Record<string, string>>({});
506: 
507:   const validate = (formData: FormData) => {
508:     const newErrors: Record<string, string> = {};
509: 
510:     if (!formData.email) newErrors.email = 'Email is required';
511:     else if (!isValidEmail(formData.email)) newErrors.email = 'Invalid email format';
512: 
513:     setErrors(newErrors);
514:     return Object.keys(newErrors).length === 0;
515:   };
516: 
517:   return (
518:     <form
519:       onSubmit={(e) => {
520:         e.preventDefault();
521:         const formData = new FormData(e.currentTarget);
522:         if (validate(Object.fromEntries(formData))) {
523:           // Submit
524:         }
525:       }}
526:     >
527:       <Input
528:         name="email"
529:         aria-invalid={!!errors.email}
530:         aria-describedby={errors.email ? 'email-error' : undefined}
531:       />
532:       {errors.email && (
533:         <div id="email-error" role="alert" className="error">
534:           {errors.email}
535:         </div>
536:       )}
537:     </form>
538:   );
539: };
540: ```
541: 
542: ## Summary: Pattern Implementation Checklist
543: 
544: ```markdown
545: For every component implementing a pattern:
546: 
547: ### Accessibility
548: - [ ] Appropriate ARIA roles, states, properties
549: - [ ] Keyboard navigation fully supported
550: - [ ] Focus management correct
551: - [ ] Screen reader friendly
552: - [ ] Color contrast >= 4.5:1 (AA)
553: - [ ] Touch target >= 44x44px
554: 
555: ### Usability
556: - [ ] Clear visual feedback for all states
557: - [ ] Consistent with platform conventions
558: - [ ] Error messages helpful and actionable
559: - [ ] No surprise focus changes
560: - [ ] Logical tab order
561: 
562: ### Performance
563: - [ ] Minimal re-renders
564: - [ ] Efficient event handlers
565: - [ ] Optimized animations
566: - [ ] Responsive at all breakpoints
567: 
568: ### Testing
569: - [ ] Unit tests for logic
570: - [ ] Integration tests for interactions
571: - [ ] a11y tests with axe
572: - [ ] Visual regression tests
573: - [ ] Manual keyboard testing
574: - [ ] Screen reader testing
575: ```
576: 
