 4: ---
 5: 
 6: # Hallmark Bridge Skill
 7: 
 8: Use this skill when you want stronger visual differentiation in hero/landing explorations while keeping BoostDesign quality gates.
 9: 
10: ## Purpose
11: - Combine Hallmark visual generation/redesign capability with BoostDesign governance.
12: - Prevent visual drift by normalizing outputs into design tokens and accessibility checks.
13: - Keep Hallmark optional and scoped to exploratory visual work.
14: 
15: ## External Dependency
16: - Install Hallmark engine:
17:   - `npx skills add nutlope/hallmark`
18: - Project source:
19:   - https://github.com/Nutlope/hallmark
20: 
21: ## Bridge Workflow
22: 1. Visual Exploration
23: - Use Hallmark verbs (`default`, `audit`, `redesign`, `study`) to generate direction.
24: 
25: 2. Token Normalization
26: - Pass visual output to `@design-system-architect`.
27: - Extract semantic colors, typography pairings, spacing rhythm, and component rules.
28: 
29: 3. UX Governance
30: - Validate with `@ux-ui-expert` and `ux-audit`.
31: - Ensure WCAG AA targets, component state completeness, and consistency constraints.
32: 
33: 4. Production Handoff
34: - Persist outputs in `docs/design-tokens/`.
35: - Document decisions in templates/spec artifacts.
36: 
37: ## Output Contract
38: - Visual intent summary.
39: - Token mapping proposal.
40: - Accessibility and consistency risk list.
41: - Remediation actions for non-compliant visual choices.
42: 
43: ## Guardrails
44: - Hallmark output cannot bypass BoostDesign accessibility checks.
45: - Hallmark output cannot replace token-driven implementation rules.
46: - If conflict exists, BoostDesign governance has precedence.
47: 
48: ## Related Artifacts
49: - `references/integration-playbook.md`
50: - `specs/hallmark-bridge-spec.md`
51: - `templates/hallmark-handoff.md`
52: - `examples/hallmark-to-ux-flow.md`
