<file path="specs/mcpee-boost-mcpee-backend/specs/clean-architecture.md">
 1: # Clean Architecture Spec
 2: 
 3: ## Purpose
 4: 
 5: Preserve directional boundaries so backend business rules remain independent from delivery and infrastructure concerns.
 6: 
 7: This spec represents universal backend boost knowledge. It must not contain customer-specific documentation or project-specific one-off decisions.
 8: 
 9: ## Principles
10: 
11: - Domain rules must not depend on framework or infrastructure implementation details.
12: - Application use-cases orchestrate workflows through interfaces, not concrete adapters.
13: - Infrastructure concerns remain replaceable and isolated behind ports/adapters.
14: 
15: ## Validation Rules
16: 
17: - Dependency direction always points inward toward domain/application layers.
18: - Controllers and handlers do not access persistence details directly.
19: - Cross-layer communication contracts are explicit and testable.
20: 
21: ## Anti-Patterns
22: 
23: - Domain services importing infrastructure entities or repositories directly.
24: - Transport/controller logic containing business decision rules.
25: - Adapters driving use-case orchestration instead of application services.
26: 
27: ## Evidence Required
28: 
29: Use import/dependency graphs, call paths, and test boundaries to verify architectural direction.
30: 
