<file path="specs/mcpee-boost-mcpee-backend/specs/versioning.md">
 1: # Versioning Spec
 2: 
 3: ## Purpose
 4: 
 5: Define explicit version evolution rules that protect clients while enabling backend change.
 6: 
 7: This spec represents universal backend boost knowledge. It must not contain customer-specific documentation or project-specific one-off decisions.
 8: 
 9: ## Principles
10: 
11: - Treat contract evolution as a planned compatibility process.
12: - Document deprecations with timelines, migration guidance, and consumer communication.
13: - Automate compatibility verification through tests and policy checks.
14: 
15: ## Validation Rules
16: 
17: - Breaking changes require explicit version transition strategy and rollout sequencing.
18: - Consumer-visible behavior changes are tested against previous supported versions.
19: - Deprecation metadata is discoverable and consistent in docs and runtime responses.
20: 
21: ## Anti-Patterns
22: 
23: - Shipping breaking changes under unchanged version contracts.
24: - Multiple versioning rules applied inconsistently across endpoints.
25: - Deprecation without migration support or sunset communication.
