124: # GitNexus — Code Intelligence
125: 
126: This project is indexed by GitNexus as **platform-tech-riders** (6605 symbols, 10984 relationships, 209 execution flows). Use the GitNexus MCP tools to understand code, assess impact, and navigate safely.
127: 
128: > Index stale? Run `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze` from the project root — it auto-selects an available runner. No `.gitnexus/run.cjs` yet? `npx gitnexus analyze` (npm 11 crash → `npm i -g gitnexus`; #1939).
129: 
130: ## Always Do
131: 
132: - **MUST run impact analysis before editing any symbol.** Before modifying a function, class, or method, run `impact({target: "symbolName", direction: "upstream"})` and report the blast radius (direct callers, affected processes, risk level) to the user.
133: - **MUST run `detect_changes()` before committing** to verify your changes only affect expected symbols and execution flows. For regression review, compare against the default branch: `detect_changes({scope: "compare", base_ref: "main"})`.
134: - **MUST warn the user** if impact analysis returns HIGH or CRITICAL risk before proceeding with edits.
135: - When exploring unfamiliar code, use `query({search_query: "concept"})` to find execution flows instead of grepping. It returns process-grouped results ranked by relevance.
136: - When you need full context on a specific symbol — callers, callees, which execution flows it participates in — use `context({name: "symbolName"})`.
137: - For security review, `explain({target: "fileOrSymbol"})` lists taint findings (source→sink flows; needs `analyze --pdg`).
138: 
139: ## Never Do
140: 
141: - NEVER edit a function, class, or method without first running `impact` on it.
142: - NEVER ignore HIGH or CRITICAL risk warnings from impact analysis.
143: - NEVER rename symbols with find-and-replace — use `rename` which understands the call graph.
144: - NEVER commit changes without running `detect_changes()` to check affected scope.
145: 
146: ## Resources
147: 
148: | Resource | Use for |
149: |----------|---------|
150: | `gitnexus://repo/platform-tech-riders/context` | Codebase overview, check index freshness |
151: | `gitnexus://repo/platform-tech-riders/clusters` | All functional areas |
152: | `gitnexus://repo/platform-tech-riders/processes` | All execution flows |
153: | `gitnexus://repo/platform-tech-riders/process/{name}` | Step-by-step execution trace |
154: 
155: ## CLI
156: 
157: | Task | Read this skill file |
158: |------|---------------------|
159: | Understand architecture / "How does X work?" | `.claude/skills/gitnexus/gitnexus-exploring/SKILL.md` |
160: | Blast radius / "What breaks if I change X?" | `.claude/skills/gitnexus/gitnexus-impact-analysis/SKILL.md` |
161: | Trace bugs / "Why is X failing?" | `.claude/skills/gitnexus/gitnexus-debugging/SKILL.md` |
162: | Rename / extract / split / refactor | `.claude/skills/gitnexus/gitnexus-refactoring/SKILL.md` |
163: | Tools, resources, schema reference | `.claude/skills/gitnexus/gitnexus-guide/SKILL.md` |
